[2004.828706, "o", "\u001b[4mFIND\u001b[24m(1)                                                     General Commands Manual                                                    \u001b[4mFIND\u001b[24m(1)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       find - search for files in a directory hierarchy\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mSYNOPSIS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22m[-H] [-L] [-P] [-D debugopts] [-Olevel] [starting-point...] [expression]\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       This manual page documents the GNU version of \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.  GNU \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22msearches the directory tree rooted at each given starting-point by evalu‐\u001b[m\r\n       ating the given expression from left to right, according to the rules of precedence (see section OPERATORS), until the outcome is known\u001b[m\r\n       (the  left  hand  side  is false for \u001b[4mand\u001b[24m operations, true for \u001b[4mor\u001b[24m), at which point \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mmoves on to the next file name.  If no starting-\u001b[m\r\n       point is specified, `.' is assumed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       If you are using \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22min an environment where security is important (for example if you are using it to  search  directories  that  are\u001b[m\r\n       writable by other users), you should read the `Security Considerations' chapter of the findutils documentation, which is called \u001b[1mFinding\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[1mFiles \u001b[22mand comes with findutils.  That document also includes a lot more detail and discussion than this manual page, so you may find it\u001b[m\r\n       a more useful source of information.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mOPTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       The  \u001b[1m-H\u001b[22m,  \u001b[1m-L  \u001b[22mand  \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22moptions control the treatment of symbolic links.  Command-line arguments following these are taken to be names of\u001b[m\r\n       files or directories to be examined, up to the first argument that begins with `-', or the argument `(' or `!'.  That argument and  any\u001b[m\r\n       following arguments are taken to be the expression describing what is to be searched for.  If no paths are given, the current directory\u001b[m\r\n       is used.  If no expression is given, the expression \u001b[1m-print \u001b[22mis used (but you should probably consider using \u001b[1m-print0 \u001b[22minstead, anyway).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       This manual page talks about `options' within the expression list.  These options control the behaviour of \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mbut are specified imme‐\u001b[m\r\n       diately  after the last path name.  The five `real' options \u001b[1m-H\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-L\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-P\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-D \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-O \u001b[22mmust appear before the first path name, if at all.  A\u001b[m\r\n       double dash \u001b[1m-- \u001b[22mcould theoretically be used to signal that any remaining arguments are not options, but this does not really work due to\u001b[m\r\n       the way \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mdetermines the end of the following path arguments: it does that by reading until an expression argument comes (which also\u001b[m\r\n       starts with a `-').  Now, if a path argument would start with a `-', then \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwould treat it as expression argument instead.  Thus, to\u001b[m\r\n       ensure that all start points are taken as such, and especially to prevent that wildcard patterns expanded by the calling shell are  not\u001b[m\r\n       mistakenly  t"]
[2004.828938, "o", "reated as expression arguments, it is generally safer to prefix wildcards or dubious path names with either `./' or to use\u001b[m\r\n       absolute path names starting with '/'.  Alternatively, it is generally safe though non-portable to use the GNU option  \u001b[1m-files0-from  \u001b[22mto\u001b[m\r\n       pass arbitrary starting points to \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       -P     Never follow symbolic links.  This is the default behaviour.  When \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mexamines or prints information about files, and the file\u001b[m\r\n              is a symbolic link, the information used shall be taken from the properties of the symbolic link itself.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       -L     Follow symbolic links.  When \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mexamines or prints information about files, the information used shall be taken from the prop‐\u001b[m\r\n              erties  of the file to which the link points, not from the link itself (unless it is a broken symbolic link or \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mis unable to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.566128, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.566984, "o", "              examine the file to which the link points).  Use of this option implies \u001b[1m-noleaf\u001b[22m.  If you later use the \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22moption,  \u001b[1m-noleaf  \u001b[22mwill\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 2 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              still be in effect.  If \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mis in effect and \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mdiscovers a symbolic link to a subdirectory during its search, the subdirectory\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 3 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              pointed to by the symbolic link will be searched.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 4 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 5 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              When  the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption is in effect, the \u001b[1m-type \u001b[22mpredicate will always match against the type of the file that a symbolic link points\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 6 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              to rather than the link itself (unless the symbolic link is broken).  Actions that can cause symbolic  links  to  become  broken\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 7 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              while  \u001b[1mfind  \u001b[22mis  executing  (for  example \u001b[1m-delete\u001b[22m) can give rise to confusing behaviour.  Using \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mcauses the \u001b[1m-lname \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-ilname\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 8 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              predicates always to return false.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 9 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 10 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -H     Do not follow symbolic links, except while processing the command line arguments.  When  \u001b[1mfind  \u001b[22mexamines  or  prints  information\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 11 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              about  files,  the  information used shall be taken from the properties of the symbolic link itself.  The only exception to this\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 12 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.567467, "o", "              behaviour is when a file specified on the command line is a symbolic link, and the link can be resolved.   For  that  situation,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 13 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the  information used is taken from whatever the link points to (that is, the link is followed).  The information about the link\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 14 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              itself is used as a fallback if the file pointed to by the symbolic link cannot be examined.  If \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22mis in effect and one of  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 15 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              paths  specified  on the command line is a symbolic link to a directory, the contents of that directory will be examined (though\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 16 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              of course \u001b[1m-maxdepth 0 \u001b[22mwould prevent this).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 17 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 18 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       If more than one of \u001b[1m-H\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22mis specified, each overrides the others; the last one appearing on the  command  line  takes  effect.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 19 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Since it is the default, the \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22moption should be considered to be in effect unless either \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mis specified.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 20 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.56785, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 21 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       GNU  \u001b[1mfind  \u001b[22mfrequently stats files during the processing of the command line itself, before any searching has begun.  These options also\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 22 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       affect how those arguments are processed.  Specifically, there are a number of tests that compare files  listed  on  the  command  line\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 23 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       against  a file we are currently considering.  In each case, the file specified on the command line will have been examined and some of\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 24 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       its properties will have been saved.  If the named file is in fact a symbolic link, and the \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22moption is in effect (or  if  neither  \u001b[1m-H\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 25 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.568048, "o", "       nor  \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mwere specified), the information used for the comparison will be taken from the properties of the symbolic link.  Otherwise, it\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 26 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       will be taken from the properties of the file the link points to.  If \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mcannot follow the link (for example because it has  insuffi‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 27 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       cient privileges or the link points to a nonexistent file) the properties of the link itself will be used.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 28 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.568203, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 29 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       When  the  \u001b[1m-H  \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moptions are in effect, any symbolic links listed as the argument of \u001b[1m-newer \u001b[22mwill be dereferenced, and the timestamp\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 30 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       will be taken from the file to which the symbolic link points.  The same consideration applies to \u001b[1m-newerXY\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-anewer \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-cnewer\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 31 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.568625, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 32 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22moption has a similar effect to \u001b[1m-L\u001b[22m, though it takes effect at the point where it appears (that is, if \u001b[1m-L  \u001b[22mis  not  used  but\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 33 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.568876, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22mis, any symbolic links appearing after \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22mon the command line will be dereferenced, and those before it will not).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 34 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 35 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -D debugopts\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 36 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Print  diagnostic  information;  this can be helpful to diagnose problems with why \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mis not doing what you want.  The list of\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 37 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              debug options should be comma separated.  Compatibility of the debug options is not guaranteed between  releases  of  findutils.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 38 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              For a complete list of valid debug options, see the output of \u001b[1mfind -D help\u001b[22m.  Valid debug options include\u001b[m\r\n\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 40 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              exec   Show diagnostic information relating to -exec, -execdir, -ok and -okdir\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 41 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 42 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.568998, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              opt    Prints diagnostic information relating to the optimisation of the expression tree; see the -O option.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 43 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 44 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.56925, "o", "              rates  Prints a summary indicating how often each predicate succeeded or failed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 45 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 46 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              search Navigate the directory tree verbosely.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 47 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 48 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.569434, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              stat   Print  messages  as  files  are  examined  with the \u001b[1mstat \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mlstat \u001b[22msystem calls.  The \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mprogram tries to minimise such\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 49 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     calls.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 50 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 51 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tree   Show the expression tree in its original and optimized form.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 52 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 53 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.569686, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              all    Enable all of the other debug options (but \u001b[1mhelp\u001b[22m).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 54 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 55 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              help   Explain the debugging options.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 56 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 57 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -Olevel\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 58 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Enables query optimisation.  The \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mprogram reorders tests to speed up execution while preserving the overall effect; that is,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 59 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.569882, "o", "              predicates with side effects are not reordered relative to each other.  The optimisations performed at each  optimisation  level\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 60 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              are as follows.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 61 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 62 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              0      Equivalent to optimisation level 1.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 63 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 64 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.570066, "o", "              1      This  is  the default optimisation level and corresponds to the traditional behaviour.  Expressions are reordered so that\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 65 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     tests based only on the names of files (for example \u001b[1m-name \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-regex\u001b[22m) are performed first.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 66 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 67 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              2      Any \u001b[1m-type \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-xtype \u001b[22mtests are performed after any tests based only on the names of files, but before any tests  that  re‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 68 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.570225, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     quire  information  from  the  inode.  On many modern versions of Unix, file types are returned by \u001b[1mreaddir() \u001b[22mand so these\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 69 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     predicates are faster to evaluate than predicates which need to stat the file first.  If you use the  \u001b[1m-fstype \u001b[4m\u001b[22mFOO\u001b[24m  predi‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 70 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     cate and specify a filesystem type \u001b[4mFOO\u001b[24m which is not known (that is, present in `/etc/mtab') at the time \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mstarts, that\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 71 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.570429, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     predicate is equivalent to \u001b[1m-false\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 72 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 73 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              3      At this optimisation level, the full cost-based query optimizer is enabled.  The order of tests is modified so that cheap\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 74 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     (i.e.  fast) tests are performed first and more expensive ones are performed later, if necessary.  Within each cost band,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 75 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.570608, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     predicates are evaluated earlier or later according to whether they are likely to succeed or  not.   For  \u001b[1m-o\u001b[22m,  predicates\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 76 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     which are likely to succeed are evaluated earlier, and for \u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m, predicates which are likely to fail are evaluated earlier.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 77 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.570841, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 78 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The  cost-based  optimizer has a fixed idea of how likely any given test is to succeed.  In some cases the probability takes ac‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 79 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              count of the specific nature of the test (for example, \u001b[1m-type f \u001b[22mis assumed to be more likely to succeed than \u001b[1m-type c\u001b[22m).  The cost-\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 80 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              based optimizer is currently being evaluated.  If it does not actually improve the performance  of  \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m,  it  will  be  removed\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 81 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              again.   Conversely,  optimisations  that prove to be reliable, robust and effective may be enabled at lower optimisation levels\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 82 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.570947, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              over time.  However, the default behaviour (i.e. optimisation level 1) will not be changed in the  4.3.x  release  series.   The\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 83 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              findutils test suite runs all the tests on \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mat each optimisation level and ensures that the result is the same.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 84 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.571182, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 85 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The  re-ordering  of operations performed by the cost-based optimizer can result in user-visible behaviour change.  For example,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 86 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the \u001b[1m-readable \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-empty \u001b[22mpredicates are sensitive to re-ordering.  If they are run in the order \u001b[1m-empty -readable\u001b[22m, an error  mes‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 87 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              sage  will be issued for unreadable directories.  If they are run in the order \u001b[1m-readable -empty \u001b[22mno error message will be issued.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 88 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.571289, "o", "              This is the reason why such operation re-ordering is not performed at the default optimisation level.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 89 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 90 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[1mEXPRESSION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 91 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.5939, "o", "       The part of the command line after the list of starting points is the \u001b[4mexpression\u001b[24m.  This is a kind of query specification describing how\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 92 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       we match files and what we do with the files that were matched.  An expression is composed of a sequence of things:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 93 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 94 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.594124, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Tests  Tests return a true or false value, usually on the basis of some property of a file we are considering.  The \u001b[1m-empty \u001b[22mtest for ex‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 95 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ample is true only when the current file is empty.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 96 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 97 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Actions\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 98 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Actions have side effects (such as printing something on the standard output) and return either true or false, usually based  on\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 99 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              whether or not they are successful.  The \u001b[1m-print \u001b[22maction for example prints the name of the current file on the standard output.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 100 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 101 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Global options\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 102 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Global  options  affect the operation of tests and actions specified on any part of the command line.  Global options always re‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 103 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              turn true.  The \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22moption for example makes \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mtraverse the file system in a depth-first order.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 104 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 105 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Positional options\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 106 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Positional options affect only tests or actions which follow them.  Positional options always return true.  The  \u001b[1m-regextype  \u001b[22mop‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 107 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tion for example is positional, specifying the regular expression dialect for regular expressions occurring later on the command\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 108 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              line.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 109 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 110 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Operators\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 111 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Operators join together the other items within the expression.  They include for example \u001b[1m-o \u001b[22m(meaning logical OR) and \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22m(meaning\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 112 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              logical AND).  Where an operator is missing, \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mis assumed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 113 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 114 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The  \u001b[1m-print  \u001b[22maction is performed on all files for which the whole expression is true, unless it contains an action other than \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mor\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 115 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-quit\u001b[22m.  Actions which inhibit the default \u001b[1m-print \u001b[22mare \u001b[1m-delete\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-exec\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-execdir\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-ok\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-okdir\u001b[22"]
[2006.594354, "o", "m, \u001b[1m-fls\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-fprint\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-fprintf\u001b[22m,  \u001b[1m-ls\u001b[22m,  \u001b[1m-print  \u001b[22mand\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 116 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-printf\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 117 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 118 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction also acts like an option (since it implies \u001b[1m-depth\u001b[22m).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 119 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 120 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mPOSITIONAL OPTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 121 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Positional options always return true.  They affect only tests occurring later on the command line.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 122 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 123 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -daystart\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 124 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Measure  times  (for \u001b[1m-amin\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-atime\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-cmin\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-ctime\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-mmin\u001b[22m, and \u001b[1m-mtime\u001b[22m) from the beginning of today rather than from 24 hours ago.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 125 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              This option only affects tests which appear later on the command line.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 126 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 127 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -follow\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 128 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Deprecated; use the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption instead.  Dereference symbolic links.  Implies \u001b[1m-noleaf\u001b[22m.  The \u001b[1m-follow  \u001b[22moption  affects  only  those\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 129 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tests which appear after it on the command line.  Unless the \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption has been specified, the position of the \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22mop‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 130 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tion  changes the behaviour of the \u001b[1m-newer \u001b[22mpredicate; any files listed as the argument of \u001b[1m-newer \u001b[22mwill be dereferenced if they are\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 131 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              symbolic links.  The same consideration applies to \u001b[1m-newerXY\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-anewer \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-cnewer\u001b[22m.  Similarly, the \u001b[1m-type  \u001b[22mpredicate  will  always\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 132 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              match  against the type of the file that a symbolic link points to rather than the link itself.  Using \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22mcauses the \u001b[1m-lname\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 133 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mand -ilname \u001b[22mpredicates always to return false.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 134 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 135 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -regextype \u001b[4mtype\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 136 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Changes the regular expression syntax understood by \u001b[1m-regex \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-iregex \u001b[22mtests which occur later on  the  command  line.   To  see\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Man"]
[2006.596004, "o", "ual page find(1) line 137 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              which regular expression types are known, use \u001b[1m-regextype help\u001b[22m.  The Texinfo documentation (see \u001b[1mSEE ALSO\u001b[22m) explains the meaning of\u001b[m\r\n\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              and  differences between the various types of regular expression.  If you do not use this option, find behaves as if the regular\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 139 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              expression type \u001b[1memacs \u001b[22mhad been specified.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 140 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 141 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -warn, -nowarn\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 142 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Turn warning messages on or off.  These warnings apply only to the command line usage, not to any conditions that \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mmight en‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 143 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              counter when it searches directories.  The default behaviour corresponds to \u001b[1m-warn \u001b[22mif standard input is a  tty,  and  to  \u001b[1m-nowarn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 144 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              otherwise.   If  a  warning message relating to command-line usage is produced, the exit status of \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mis not affected.  If the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 145 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22menvironment variable is set, and \u001b[1m-warn \u001b[22mis also used, it is not specified which, if any, warnings will be active.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 146 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 147 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mGLOBAL OPTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 148 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Global options always return true.  Global options take effect even for tests which occur earlier on the command line.  To prevent con‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 149 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       fusion, global options should be specified on the command-line after the list of start points, just before the first  test,  positional\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 150 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       option  or  action.   If you specify a global option in some other place, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwill issue a warning message explaining that this can be\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 151 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       confusing.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 152 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 153 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The global options occur after the list of start points, and so are not the same kind of option as \u001b[1m-L\u001b[22m, for example.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 154 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 155 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -d     A synonym for -depth, for compatibility with FreeBSD, NetBSD, MacOS X and OpenBSD.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 156 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 157 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -depth Process each directory's contents before the directory itself.  The -delete action also implies \u001b[1m-depth\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 158 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 159 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -files0-from \u001b[4mfile\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 160 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Read the starting points from \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m instead of getting them on the command line.  In contrast to the known limitations of passing\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 161 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              starting points via arguments on the command line, namely the limitation of the amount of file names, and the inherent ambiguity\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 162 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              of file names clashing with option names, using this option allows to safely pass an arbitrary  number  of  starting  points  to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 163 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 164 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 165 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Using  this  option  and  passing starting points on the command line is mutually exclusive, and is therefore not allowed at the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 166 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              same time.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 167 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 168 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m argument is mandatory.  One can use \u001b[1m-files0-from - \u001b[22mto read the list of starting points from the \u001b[4mstandard\u001b[24m \u001b[4minput\u001b[24m  stream,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 169 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              and  e.g.  from  a  pipe.  In this case, the actions \u001b[1m-ok \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-okdir \u001b[22mare not allowed, because they would obviously interfere with\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 170 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              reading from \u001b[4mstandard\u001b[24m \u001b[4minput\u001b[24m in order to get a user confirmation.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 171 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 172 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The starting points in \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m have to be separated by ASCII NUL characters.  Two consecutive  NUL  characters,  i.e.,  a  starting\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 173 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              point with a Zero-length file name is not allowed and will lead to an error diagnostic followed by a non-Zero exit code later.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 174 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 175 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              In  the case the given \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m is empty, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mdoes not process any starting point and therefore will exit immediately after parsing\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 176 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the program arguments.  This is unlike the standard invocation where \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22massumes the current directory as starting point if  no\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 177 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              path argument is passed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 178 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n"]
[2006.596271, "o", "\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 179 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The  processing  of the starting points is otherwise as usual, e.g.  \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwill recurse into subdirectories unless otherwise pre‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 180 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              vented.  To process only the starting points, one can additionally pass \u001b[1m-maxdepth 0\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 181 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 182 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Further notes: if a file is listed more than once in the input file, it is unspecified whether it is visited more than once.  If\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 183 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m is mutated during the operation of \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m, the result is unspecified as well.  Finally,  the  seek  position  within  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 184 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              named  \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m  at  the time \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mexits, be it with \u001b[1m-quit \u001b[22mor in any other way, is also unspecified.  By \"unspecified\" here is meant\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 185 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              that it may or may not work or do any specific thing, and that the behavior may change from platform to platform, or from \u001b[1mfindu‐\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 186 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mtils \u001b[22mrelease to release.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 187 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 188 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -help, --help\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 189 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Print a summary of the command-line usage of \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mand exit.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 190 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 191 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -ignore_readdir_race\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 192 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Normally, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwill emit an error message when it fails to stat a file.  If you give this option and a file is  deleted  between\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 193 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the time \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mreads the name of the file from the directory and the time it tries to stat the file, no error message will be is‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 194 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              sued.   This  also  applies  to files or directories whose names are given on the command line.  This option takes effect at the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 195 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              time the command line is read, which means that you cannot search one part of the filesystem with this option on and part of  it\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 196 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              with  this  option  off  (if  you need to do that, you will need to issue two \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mcommands instead, one with the option and one\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 197 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              without it).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 198 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 199 (press h for help"]
[2006.596415, "o", " or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Furthermore, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwith the \u001b[1m-ignore_readdir_race \u001b[22moption will ignore errors of the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction in the case the file has  disap‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 200 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              peared  since  the  parent directory was read: it will not output an error diagnostic, and the return code of the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 201 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              will be true.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 202 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 203 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -maxdepth \u001b[4mlevels\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 204 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Descend at most \u001b[4mlevels\u001b[24m (a non-negative integer) levels of directories below the starting-points.  Using \u001b[1m-maxdepth 0  \u001b[22mmeans  only\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 205 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              apply the tests and actions to the starting-points themselves.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 206 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 207 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -mindepth \u001b[4mlevels\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 208 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Do  not  apply  any  tests  or actions at levels less than \u001b[4mlevels\u001b[24m (a non-negative integer).  Using \u001b[1m-mindepth 1 \u001b[22mmeans process all\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 209 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              files except the starting-points.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 210 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 211 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -mount Don't descend directories on other filesystems.  An alternate name for \u001b[1m-xdev\u001b[22m, for compatibility  with  some  other  versions  of\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 212 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 213 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 214 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -noignore_readdir_race\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 215 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Turns off the effect of \u001b[1m-ignore_readdir_race\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 216 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 217 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -noleaf\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 218 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Do  not  optimize by assuming that directories contain 2 fewer subdirectories than their hard link count.  This option is needed\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 219 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              when searching filesystems that do not follow the Unix directory-link convention, such as CD-ROM or MS-DOS  filesystems  or  AFS\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 220 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              volume  mount  points.  Each directory on a normal Unix filesystem has at least 2 hard links: its name and its `.' entry.  Addi‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 221 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tionally, it"]
[2006.596504, "o", "s subdirectories (if any) each have a `..' entry linked to that directory.  When \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mis examining a directory,  af‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 222 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ter  it  has statted 2 fewer subdirectories than the directory's link count, it knows that the rest of the entries in the direc‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 223 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tory are non-directories (`leaf' files in the directory tree).  If only the files' names need to be examined, there is  no  need\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 224 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              to stat them; this gives a significant increase in search speed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 225 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 226 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -version, --version\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 227 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Print the \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mversion number and exit.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 228 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 229 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -xdev  Don't descend directories on other filesystems.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 230 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 231 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mTESTS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 232 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Some  tests,  for  example  \u001b[1m-newerXY  \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-samefile\u001b[22m, allow comparison between the file currently being examined and some reference file\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 233 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       specified on the command line.  When these tests are used, the interpretation of the reference file is determined by the options \u001b[1m-H\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-L\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 234 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       and \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22mand any previous \u001b[1m-follow\u001b[22m, but the reference file is only examined once, at the time the command line is parsed.  If  the  refer‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 235 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       ence  file  cannot  be  examined (for example, the \u001b[1mstat\u001b[22m(2) system call fails for it), an error message is issued, and \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mexits with a\u001b[m\r\n\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       nonzero status.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 237 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 238 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       A numeric argument \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m can be specified to tests (like \u001b[1m-amin\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-mtime\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-gid\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-inum\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-links\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-size\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-uid \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-used\u001b[22m) as\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 239 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 240 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4m+n\u001b[24m     for greater than \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 241 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 242 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4m-n\u001b[24m     for less than \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 243 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 244 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\b"]
[2006.596671, "o", "B\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m      for exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 245 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 246 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Supported tests:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 247 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 248 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -amin \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 249 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File was last accessed less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m minutes ago.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 250 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 251 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -anewer \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 252 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Time of the last access of the current file is more recent than that of the last data modification of the  \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m  file.   If\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 253 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m is a symbolic link and the \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22moption or the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption is in effect, then the time of the last data modification of the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 254 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              file it points to is always used.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 255 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 256 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -atime \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 257 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File  was  last accessed less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m*24 hours ago.  When \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mfigures out how many 24-hour periods ago the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 258 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              file was last accessed, any fractional part is ignored, so to match \u001b[1m-atime +1\u001b[22m, a file has to have been  accessed  at  least  \u001b[4mtwo\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 259 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              days ago.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 260 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 261 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -cmin \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 262 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File's status was last changed less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m minutes ago.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 263 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 264 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -cnewer \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 265 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Time of the last status change of the current file is more recent than that of the last data modification of the \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m file.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 266 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              If  \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m is a symbolic link and the \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22moption or the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption is in effect, then the time of the last data modification of\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 267 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the file it points to is always used.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 268 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 269 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -ctime \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 270 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File's status was last changed less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m*24 hours ago.  See the comments for \u001b[1m-atime  \u001b[22mto  understand  how\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 271 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              rounding affects the interpretation of file status change times.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 272 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 273 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -empty File is empty and is either a regular file or a directory.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 274 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 275 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -executable\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 276 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Matches  files  which are executable and directories which are searchable (in a file name resolution sense) by the current user.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 277 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              This takes into account access control lists and other permissions artefacts which the \u001b[1m-perm \u001b[22mtest ignores.  This test makes  use\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 278 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              of  the  \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) system call, and so can be fooled by NFS servers which do UID mapping (or root-squashing), since many systems\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 279 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              implement \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) in the client's kernel and so cannot make use of the UID mapping information held on  the  server.   Because\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 280 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              this  test  is based only on the result of the \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) system call, there is no guarantee that a file for which this test suc‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 281 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ceeds can actually be executed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 282 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 283 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -false Always false.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 284 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 285 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -fstype \u001b[4mtype\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 286 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File is on a filesystem of type \u001b[4mtype\u001b[24m.  The valid filesystem types vary among different versions of Unix; an incomplete  list  of\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 287 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              filesystem types that are accepted on some version of Unix or another is: ufs, 4.2, 4.3, nfs, tmp, mfs, S51K, S52K.  You can use\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 288 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1m-printf \u001b[22mwith the %F directive to see the types of your filesystems.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 289 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 290 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -gid \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m File's numeric group ID is less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 291 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 292 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -group \u001b[4mgname\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 293 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.596754, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File belongs to group \u001b[4mgname\u001b[24m (numeric group ID allowed).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 294 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 295 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -ilname \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 296 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Like  \u001b[1m-lname\u001b[22m,  but  the match is case insensitive.  If the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption or the \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22moption is in effect, this test returns false\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 297 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              unless the symbolic link is broken.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 298 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 299 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -iname \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 300 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.596898, "o", "              Like \u001b[1m-name\u001b[22m, but the match is case insensitive.  For example, the patterns `fo*' and `F??' match the  file  names  `Foo',  `FOO',\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 301 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `foo', `fOo', etc.  The pattern `*foo*` will also match a file called '.foobar'.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 302 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 303 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -inum \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 304 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File has inode number smaller than, greater than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m.  It is normally easier to use the \u001b[1m-samefile \u001b[22mtest instead.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 305 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 306 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
