[2006.597158, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 318 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -lname \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 319 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File  is  a symbolic link whose contents match shell pattern \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.  The metacharacters do not treat `/' or `.' specially.  If\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 320 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.597214, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption or the \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22moption is in effect, this test returns false unless the symbolic link is broken.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 321 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 322 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.597374, "o", "       -mmin \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 323 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File's data was last modified less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m minutes ago.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 324 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 325 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -mtime \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 326 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File's data was last modified less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m*24 hours ago.  See the comments for  \u001b[1m-atime  \u001b[22mto  understand  how\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 327 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              rounding affects the interpretation of file modification times.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 328 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 329 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -name \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 330 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.597433, "o", "              Base  of  file name (the path with the leading directories removed) matches shell pattern \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.  Because the leading directo‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 331 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ries of the file names are removed, the \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m should not include a slash, because `-name a/b' will never match  anything  (and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 332 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.597575, "o", "              you  probably  want to use \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22minstead).  An exception to this is when using only a slash as \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m (`-name /'), because that\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 333 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              is a valid string for matching the root directory \"/\" (because the base name of \"/\" is \"/\").  A warning is issued if you try  to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 334 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              pass  a  pattern containing a - but not consisting solely of one - slash, unless the environment variable \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22mis set\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 335 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              or the option \u001b[1m-nowarn \u001b[22mis used.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 336 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 337 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.597744, "o", "              To ignore a directory and the files under it, use \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mrather than checking every file in the tree; see an example in the  de‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 338 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              scription  of  that  action.  Braces are not recognised as being special, despite the fact that some shells including Bash imbue\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 339 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              braces with a special meaning in shell patterns.  The filename matching is performed with the  use  of  the  \u001b[1mfnmatch\u001b[22m(3)  library\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 340 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              function.  Don't forget to enclose the pattern in quotes in order to protect it from expansion by the shell.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 341 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 342 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.597866, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -newer \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 343 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Time  of  the last data modification of the current file is more recent than that of the last data modification of the \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 344 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.597984, "o", "              file.  If \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m is a symbolic link and the \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22moption or the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption is in effect, then the time of the last data modifica‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 345 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tion of the file it points to is always used.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 346 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 347 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -newerXY \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 348 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.598137, "o", "              Succeeds if timestamp \u001b[4mX\u001b[24m of the file being considered is newer than timestamp \u001b[4mY\u001b[24m of the file \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m.  The letters \u001b[4mX\u001b[24m and  \u001b[4mY\u001b[24m  can\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 349 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              be any of the following letters:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 350 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 351 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              a   The access time of the file \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 352 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              B   The birth time of the file \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 353 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.598227, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              c   The inode status change time of \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 354 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              m   The modification time of the file \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 355 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              t   \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m is interpreted directly as a time\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 356 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 357 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Some  combinations are invalid; for example, it is invalid for \u001b[4mX\u001b[24m to be \u001b[4mt\u001b[24m.  Some combinations are not implemented on all systems;\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 358 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.598312, "o", "              for example \u001b[4mB\u001b[24m is not supported on all systems.  If an invalid or unsupported combination of \u001b[4mXY\u001b[24m is specified, a fatal  error  re‐\u001b[m\r\n\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              sults.   Time specifications are interpreted as for the argument to the \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22moption of GNU \u001b[1mdate\u001b[22m.  If you try to use the birth time\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 360 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.598397, "o", "              of a reference file, and the birth time cannot be determined, a fatal error message results.  If you specify a test which refers\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 361 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              to the birth time of files being examined, this test will fail for any files where the birth time is unknown.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 362 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 363 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.59847, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -nogroup\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 364 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              No group corresponds to file's numeric group ID.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 365 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.598545, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 366 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -nouser\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 367 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              No user corresponds to file's numeric user ID.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 368 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 369 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.59862, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -path \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 370 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File name matches shell pattern \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.  The metacharacters do not treat `/' or `.' specially; so, for example,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 371 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.598696, "o", "                  find . -path \"./sr*sc\"\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 372 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              will print an entry for a directory called \u001b[4m./src/misc\u001b[24m (if one exists).  To ignore a whole directory tree, use \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mrather than\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 373 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              checking every file in the tree.  Note that the pattern match test applies to the whole file name,  starting  from  one  of  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 374 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.598782, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              start  points named on the command line.  It would only make sense to use an absolute path name here if the relevant start point\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 375 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              is also an absolute path.  This means that this command will never match anything:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 376 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.598856, "o", "                  find bar -path /foo/bar/myfile -print\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 377 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.598976, "o", "              Find compares the \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22margument with the concatenation of a directory name and the base name of the file it's examining.  Since\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 378 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the concatenation will never end with a slash, \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22marguments ending in a slash will match  nothing  (except  perhaps  a  start\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 379 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              point  specified  on the command line).  The predicate \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22mis also supported by HP-UX \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mand is part of the POSIX 2008 stan‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 380 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              dard.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 381 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 382 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599054, "o", "       -perm \u001b[4mmode\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 383 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File's permission bits are exactly \u001b[4mmode\u001b[24m (octal or symbolic).  Since an exact match is required, if you want to use this form for\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 384 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              symbolic modes, you may have to specify a rather complex mode string.  For example `-perm g=w' will only match files which  have\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 385 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599123, "o", "              mode  0020 (that is, ones for which group write permission is the only permission set).  It is more likely that you will want to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 386 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              use the `/' or `-' forms, for example `-perm -g=w', which matches any file with group write permission.  See the  \u001b[1mEXAMPLES  \u001b[22msec‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 387 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599194, "o", "              tion for some illustrative examples.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 388 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 389 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -perm -\u001b[4mmode\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 390 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599265, "o", "              All  of the permission bits \u001b[4mmode\u001b[24m are set for the file.  Symbolic modes are accepted in this form, and this is usually the way in\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 391 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              which you would want to use them.  You must specify `u', `g' or `o' if you use a symbolic mode.  See the  \u001b[1mEXAMPLES  \u001b[22msection  for\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 392 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599336, "o", "              some illustrative examples.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 393 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 394 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -perm /\u001b[4mmode\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 395 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599415, "o", "              Any  of  the permission bits \u001b[4mmode\u001b[24m are set for the file.  Symbolic modes are accepted in this form.  You must specify `u', `g' or\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 396 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `o' if you use a symbolic mode.  See the \u001b[1mEXAMPLES \u001b[22msection for some illustrative examples.  If no permission  bits  in  \u001b[4mmode\u001b[24m  are\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 397 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.599491, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              set, this test matches any file (the idea here is to be consistent with the behaviour of \u001b[1m-perm -000\u001b[22m).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 398 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 399 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -perm +\u001b[4mmode\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 400 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599566, "o", "              This is no longer supported (and has been deprecated since 2005).  Use \u001b[1m-perm /\u001b[4m\u001b[22mmode\u001b[24m instead.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 401 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 402 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -readable\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 403 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.599651, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Matches  files which are readable by the current user.  This takes into account access control lists and other permissions arte‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 404 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              facts which the \u001b[1m-perm \u001b[22mtest ignores.  This test makes use of the \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) system call, and so can be fooled by NFS servers which\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 405 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599737, "o", "              do UID mapping (or root-squashing), since many systems implement \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) in the client's kernel and so cannot make use of  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 406 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              UID mapping information held on the server.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 407 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 408 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599828, "o", "       -regex \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 409 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File  name  matches  regular expression \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.  This is a match on the whole path, not a search.  For example, to match a file\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 410 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599899, "o", "              named \u001b[4m./fubar3,\u001b[24m you can use the regular expression `.*bar.' or `.*b.*3', but not `f.*r3'.  The regular expressions understood by\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 411 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mare by default Emacs Regular Expressions, but this can be changed with the \u001b[1m-regextype \u001b[22moption.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 412 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 413 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -samefile \u001b[4mname\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 414 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.599963, "o", "              File refers to the same inode as \u001b[4mname\u001b[24m.  When \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mis in effect, this can include symbolic links.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 415 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 416 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -size \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m[cwbkMG]\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 417 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.600021, "o", "              File uses less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m units of space, rounding up.  The following suffixes can be used:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 418 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 419 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `b'    for 512-byte blocks (this is the default if no suffix is used)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 420 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.600085, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 421 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `c'    for bytes\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 422 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 423 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `w'    for two-byte words\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 424 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60017, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 425 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `k'    for kibibytes (KiB, units of 1024 bytes)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 426 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 427 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.600209, "o", "              `M'    for mebibytes (MiB, units of 1024 * 1024 = 1048576 bytes)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 428 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 429 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `G'    for gibibytes (GiB, units of 1024 * 1024 * 1024 = 1073741824 bytes)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 430 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 431 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The size is simply the st_size member of the struct stat populated by the lstat (or stat)  system  call,  rounded  up  as  shown\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 432 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              above.   In  other  words, it's consistent with the result you get for \u001b[1mls -l\u001b[22m.  Bear in mind that the `%k' and `%b' format speci‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 433 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.600235, "o", "              fiers of \u001b[1m-printf \u001b[22mhandle sparse files differently.  The `b' suffix always denotes 512-byte blocks  and  never  1024-byte  blocks,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 434 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60026, "o", "              which is different to the behaviour of \u001b[1m-ls\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 435 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 436 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.600286, "o", "              The  + and - prefixes signify greater than and less than, as usual; i.e., an exact size of \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m units does not match.  Bear in mind\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 437 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.600327, "o", "              that the size is rounded up to the next unit.  Therefore \u001b[1m-size -1M \u001b[22mis  not  equivalent  to  \u001b[1m-size -1048576c\u001b[22m.   The  former  only\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 438 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              matches empty files, the latter matches files from 0 to 1,048,575 bytes.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 439 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.600354, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 440 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -true  Always true.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 441 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.600392, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 442 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -type \u001b[4mc\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 443 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File is of type \u001b[4mc\u001b[24m:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 444 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.600425, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 445 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              b      block (buffered) special\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 446 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 447 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.600453, "o", "              c      character (unbuffered) special\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 448 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 449 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
