[2006.605118, "o", "ne 693 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 694 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     y      last two digits of year (00..99)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 695 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 696 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     Y      year (1970...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 697 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 698 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %b     The  amount  of  disk  space  used  for  this file in 512-byte blocks.  Since disk space is allocated in multiples of the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 699 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     filesystem block size this is usually greater than %s/512, but it can also be smaller if the file is a sparse file.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 700 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 701 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %B\u001b[4mk\u001b[24m    File's birth time, i.e., its creation time, in the format specified by \u001b[4mk\u001b[24m, which is the same as for  %A.   This  directive\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 702 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     produces an empty string if the underlying operating system or filesystem does not support birth times.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 703 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 704 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %c     File's last status change time in the format returned by the C \u001b[1mctime\u001b[22m(3) function.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 705 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 706 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %C\u001b[4mk\u001b[24m    File's last status change time in the format specified by \u001b[4mk\u001b[24m, which is the same as for %A.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 707 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 708 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %d     File's depth in the directory tree; 0 means the file is a starting-point.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 709 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 710 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %D     The device number on which the file exists (the st_dev field of struct stat), in decimal.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 711 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 712 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %f     Print  the  basename; the file's name with any leading directories removed (only the last element).  For \u001b[1m/\u001b[22m, the result is\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 713 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     `/'.  See the \u001b[1mEXAMPLES \u001b[22msection for an example.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 714 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 715 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %F     Type of the filesystem the file is on; this value can be used for -fstype.\u001b[m\r\n\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 717 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %g     File's group name, or numeric group ID if the group has no name.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 718 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 719 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %G     File's numeric group ID.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 720 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 721 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %h     Dirname; the Leading directories of the file's name (all but the last element).  If the file  name  contains  no  slashes\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 722 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     (since  it  is in the current directory) the %h specifier expands to `.'.  For files which are themselves directories and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 723 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605134, "o", "                     contain a slash (including \u001b[1m/\u001b[22m), %h expands to the empty string.  See the \u001b[1mEXAMPLES \u001b[22msection for an example.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 724 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60515, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 725 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605298, "o", "              %H     Starting-point under which file was found.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 726 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 727 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %i     File's inode number (in decimal).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 728 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605334, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 729 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %k     The amount of disk space used for this file in 1 KB blocks.  Since disk space is allocated in multiples of the filesystem\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 730 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     block size this is usually greater than %s/1024, but it can also be smaller if the file is a sparse file.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 731 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 732 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %l     Object of symbolic link (empty string if file is not a symbolic link).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 733 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 734 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %m     File's permission bits (in octal).  This option uses the `traditional' numbers which most Unix implementations  use,  but\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 735 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605352, "o", "                     if  your  particular implementation uses an unusual ordering of octal permissions bits, you will see a difference between\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 736 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     the actual value of the file's mode and the output of %m.  Normally you will want to have a leading zero on this  number,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 737 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605406, "o", "                     and to do this, you should use the \u001b[1m# \u001b[22mflag (as in, for example, `%#m').\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 738 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 739 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %M     File's permissions (in symbolic form, as for \u001b[1mls\u001b[22m).  This directive is supported in findutils 4.2.5 and later.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 740 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 741 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.605442, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605484, "o", "              %n     Number of hard links to file.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 742 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 743 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %p     File's name.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 744 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605523, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 745 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %P     File's name with the name of the starting-point under which it was found removed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 746 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 747 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.605561, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %s     File's size in bytes.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 748 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 749 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605605, "o", "              %S     File's  sparseness.  This is calculated as (BLOCKSIZE*st_blocks / st_size).  The exact value you will get for an ordinary\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 750 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     file of a certain length is system-dependent.  However, normally sparse files will have values less than 1.0,  and  files\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 751 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605645, "o", "                     which  use indirect blocks may have a value which is greater than 1.0.  In general the number of blocks used by a file is\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 752 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     file system dependent.  The value used for BLOCKSIZE is system-dependent, but is usually 512 bytes.  If the file size  is\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 753 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605677, "o", "                     zero,  the value printed is undefined.  On systems which lack support for st_blocks, a file's sparseness is assumed to be\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 754 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     1.0.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 755 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 756 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605719, "o", "              %t     File's last modification time in the format returned by the C \u001b[1mctime\u001b[22m(3) function.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 757 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 758 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605763, "o", "              %T\u001b[4mk\u001b[24m    File's last modification time in the format specified by \u001b[4mk\u001b[24m, which is the same as for %A.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 759 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 760 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %u     File's user name, or numeric user ID if the user has no name.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 761 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.605802, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 762 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %U     File's numeric user ID.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 763 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 764 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.60584, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %y     File's type (like in \u001b[1mls -l\u001b[22m), U=unknown type (shouldn't happen)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 765 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 766 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605878, "o", "              %Y     File's type (like %y), plus follow symbolic links: `L'=loop, `N'=nonexistent, `?' for any other  error  when  determining\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 767 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     the type of the target of a symbolic link.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 768 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605916, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 769 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              %Z     (SELinux only) file's security context.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 770 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 771 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.605953, "o", "              %{ %[ %(\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 772 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                     Reserved for future use.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 773 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 774 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.605991, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              A `%' character followed by any other character is discarded, but the other character is printed (don't rely on this, as further\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 775 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606028, "o", "              format characters may be introduced).  A `%' at the end of the format argument causes undefined behaviour since there is no fol‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 776 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              lowing  character.  In some locales, it may hide your door keys, while in others it may remove the final page from the novel you\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 777 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              are reading.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 778 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.606061, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 779 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The %m and %d directives support the \u001b[1m#\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m0 \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m+ \u001b[22mflags, but the other directives do not, even if they print numbers.  Numeric di‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 780 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606104, "o", "              rectives that do not support these flags include \u001b[1mG\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mU\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mb\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mD\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mk \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mn\u001b[22m.  The `-' format flag is supported and changes  the  align‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 781 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ment of a field from right-justified (which is the default) to left-justified.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 782 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.606118, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 783 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              See the \u001b[1mUNUSUAL FILENAMES \u001b[22msection for information about how unusual characters in filenames are handled.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 784 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606171, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 785 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -prune True;  if  the file is a directory, do not descend into it.  If \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22mis given, then \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mhas no effect.  Because \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22mim‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 786 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              plies \u001b[1m-depth\u001b[22m, you cannot usefully use \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22mtogether.  For example, to skip the directory \u001b[4msrc/emacs\u001b[24m and  all  files\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 787 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606209, "o", "              and directories under it, and print the names of the other files found, do something like this:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 788 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  find . -path ./src/emacs -prune -o -print\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 789 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n"]
[2006.606251, "o", "\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 790 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606272, "o", "       -quit  Exit  immediately  (with return value zero if no errors have occurred).  This is different to \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mbecause \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22monly applies\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 791 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              to the contents of pruned directories, while \u001b[1m-quit \u001b[22msimply makes \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mstop immediately.  No child processes will be left running.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 792 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606328, "o", "              Any command lines which have been built by \u001b[1m-exec ... + \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-execdir ... + \u001b[22mare invoked before the program is exited.  After  \u001b[1m-quit\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 793 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              is  executed, no more files specified on the command line will be processed.  For example, `\u001b[1mfind \u001b[4m\u001b[22m/tmp/foo\u001b[24m \u001b[4m/tmp/bar\u001b[24m \u001b[1m-print -quit\u001b[22m`\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 794 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              will print only `/tmp/foo`.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 795 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606366, "o", "              One common use of \u001b[1m-quit \u001b[22mis to stop searching the file system once we have found what we want.  For example, if we want  to  find\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 796 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.606409, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              just a single file we can do this:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 797 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  find / -name needle -print -quit\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 798 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606425, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 799 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mOPERATORS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 800 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Listed in order of decreasing precedence:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 801 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606474, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 802 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       ( \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[24m )\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 803 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Force  precedence.   Since  parentheses are special to the shell, you will normally need to quote them.  Many of the examples in\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 804 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60651, "o", "              this manual page use backslashes for this purpose: `\\(...\\)' instead of `(...)'.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 805 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606545, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 806 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       ! \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[24m True if \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[24m is false.  This character will also usually need protection from interpretation by the shell.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 807 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606588, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 808 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -not \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 809 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606648, "o", "              Same as ! \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[24m, but not POSIX compliant.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 810 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 811 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 812 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Two expressions in a row are taken to be joined with an implied \u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m; \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[24m is not evaluated if \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m is false.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 813 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606713, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 814 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m -a \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 815 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.606784, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Same as \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 816 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 817 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m -and \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 818 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606846, "o", "              Same as \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[24m, but not POSIX compliant.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 819 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 820 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m -o \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 821 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.606934, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Or; \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[24m is not evaluated if \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m is true.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 822 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 823 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.606987, "o", "       \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m -or \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 824 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Same as \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m \u001b[1m-o \u001b[4m\u001b[22mexpr2\u001b[24m, but not POSIX compliant.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 825 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 826 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m , \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 827 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607038, "o", "              List; both \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[24m are always evaluated.  The value of \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m is discarded; the value of the list is the value of  \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 828 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The  comma  operator  can  be useful for searching for several different types of thing, but traversing the filesystem hierarchy\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 829 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607183, "o", "              only once.  The \u001b[1m-fprintf \u001b[22maction can be used to list the various matched items into several different output files.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 830 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 831 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607215, "o", "       Please note that \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mwhen specified implicitly (for example by two tests appearing without an explicit operator between them) or explic‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 832 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       itly has higher precedence than \u001b[1m-o\u001b[22m.  This means that \u001b[1mfind . -name afile -o -name bfile -print \u001b[22mwill never print \u001b[4mafile\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 833 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 834 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[1mUNUSUAL FILENAMES\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 835 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Many of the actions of \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mresult in the printing of data which is under the control of other users.  This includes file names, sizes,\u001b[m\r\n\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       modification times and so forth.  File names are a potential problem since they can contain any character except `\\0' and `/'.  Unusual\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 837 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.607243, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       characters in file names can do unexpected and often undesirable things to your terminal (for example, changing the  settings  of  your\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 838 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.607299, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607358, "o", "       function keys on some terminals).  Unusual characters are handled differently by various actions, as described below.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 839 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 840 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -print0, -fprint0\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 841 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607376, "o", "              Always print the exact filename, unchanged, even if the output is going to a terminal.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 842 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 843 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -ls, -fls\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 844 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607504, "o", "              Unusual  characters  are always escaped.  White space, backslash, and double quote characters are printed using C-style escaping\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 845 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              (for example `\\f', `\\\"').  Other unusual characters are printed using an octal escape.  Other printable characters (for \u001b[1m-ls  \u001b[22mand\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 846 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1m-fls \u001b[22mthese are the characters between octal 041 and 0176) are printed as-is.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 847 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 848 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -printf, -fprintf\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 849 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607565, "o", "              If the output is not going to a terminal, it is printed as-is.  Otherwise, the result depends on which directive is in use.  The\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 850 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              directives  %D, %F, %g, %G, %H, %Y, and %y expand to values which are not under control of files' owners, and so are printed as-\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 851 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607622, "o", "              is.  The directives %a, %b, %c, %d, %i, %k, %m, %M, %n, %s, %t, %u and %U have values which are under the control of files' own‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 852 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ers but which cannot be used to send arbitrary data to the terminal, and so these are printed as-is.  The directives %f, %h, %l,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 853 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.607642, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60773, "o", "              %p and %P are quoted.  This quoting is performed in the same way as for GNU \u001b[1mls\u001b[22m.  This is not the same quoting mechanism  as  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 854 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              one  used  for  \u001b[1m-ls \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-fls\u001b[22m.  If you are able to decide what format to use for the output of \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mthen it is normally better to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 855 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              use `\\0' as a terminator than to use newline, as file names can contain white space and newline characters.  The setting of  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 856 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607788, "o", "              \u001b[1mLC_CTYPE \u001b[22menvironment variable is used to determine which characters need to be quoted.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 857 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607865, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 858 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -print, -fprint\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 859 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Quoting  is  handled in the same way as for \u001b[1m-printf \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-fprintf\u001b[22m.  If you are using \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22min a script or in a situation where the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 860 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.607917, "o", "              matched files might have arbitrary names, you should consider using \u001b[1m-print0 \u001b[22minstead of \u001b[1m-print\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 861 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 862 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The \u001b[1m-ok \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-okdir \u001b[22mactions print the current filename as-is.  This may change in a future release.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 863 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.607969, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 864 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[1mSTANDARDS CONFORMANCE\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 865 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60803, "o", "       For closest compliance to the POSIX standard, you should set the \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22menvironment variable.  The following options are spec‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 866 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       ified in the POSIX standard (IEEE Std 1003.1-2008, 2016 Edition):\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 867 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608089, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 868 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-H     \u001b[22mThis option is supported.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 869 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 870 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60815, "o", "       \u001b[1m-L     \u001b[22mThis option is supported.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 871 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 872 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-name  \u001b[22mThis option is supported, but POSIX conformance depends on the POSIX conformance of the system's  \u001b[1mfnmatch\u001b[22m(3)  library  function.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 873 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608175, "o", "              As of findutils-4.2.2, shell metacharacters (`*', `?' or `[]' for example) match a leading `.', because IEEE PASC interpretation\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 874 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              126 requires this.  This is a change from previous versions of findutils.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 875 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 876 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.608249, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-type  \u001b[22mSupported.  POSIX specifies `b', `c', `d', `l', `p', `f' and `s'.  GNU find also supports `D', representing a Door, where the OS\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 877 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              provides these.  Furthermore, GNU find allows multiple types to be specified at once in a comma-separated list.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 878 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 879 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.608301, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60837, "o", "       \u001b[1m-ok    \u001b[22mSupported.  Interpretation of the response is according to the `yes' and `no' patterns selected by setting the \u001b[1mLC_MESSAGES \u001b[22menvi‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 880 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ronment variable.  When the \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22menvironment variable is set, these patterns are taken system's definition of a posi‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 881 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608434, "o", "              tive  (yes)  or  negative  (no)  response.  See the system's documentation for \u001b[1mnl_langinfo\u001b[22m(3), in particular YESEXPR and NOEXPR.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 882 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              When \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22mis not set, the patterns are instead taken from \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m's own message catalogue.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 883 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 884 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.608457, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-newer \u001b[22mSupported.  If the file specified is a symbolic link, it is always dereferenced.  This is  a  change  from  previous  behaviour,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 885 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              which used to take the relevant time from the symbolic link; see the HISTORY section below.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 886 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608533, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 887 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-perm  \u001b[22mSupported.   If  the \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22menvironment variable is not set, some mode arguments (for example +a+x) which are not valid\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 888 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              in POSIX are supported for backward-compatibility.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 889 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 890 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.608592, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Other primaries\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 891 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608643, "o", "              The primaries \u001b[1m-atime\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-ctime\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-depth\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-exec\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-group\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-links\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-mtime\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-nogroup\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-nouser\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-ok\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-path\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-print\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-prune\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-size\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-user\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 892 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              and \u001b[1m-xdev \u001b[22mare all supported.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 893 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.608709, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 894 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The POSIX standard specifies parentheses `(', `)', negation `!' and the logical AND/OR operators \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-o\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 895 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608745, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 896 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       All other options, predicates, expressions and so forth are extensions beyond the POSIX standard.  Many of  these  extensions  are  not\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 897 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       unique to GNU find, however.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 898 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608823, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 899 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The POSIX standard requires that \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mdetects loops:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 900 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 901 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The  \u001b[1mfind  \u001b[22mutility shall detect infinite loops; that is, entering a previously visited directory that is an ancestor of the last\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 902 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.608882, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608941, "o", "              file encountered.  When it detects an infinite loop, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mshall write a diagnostic message to standard error  and  shall  either\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 903 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              recover its position in the hierarchy or terminate.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 904 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 905 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       GNU  \u001b[1mfind  \u001b[22mcomplies  with  these requirements.  The link count of directories which contain entries which are hard links to an ancestor\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 906 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.608991, "o", "       will often be lower than they otherwise should be.  This can mean that GNU find will sometimes optimize away the visiting of  a  subdi‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 907 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609052, "o", "       rectory  which is actually a link to an ancestor.  Since \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mdoes not actually enter such a subdirectory, it is allowed to avoid emit‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 908 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       ting a diagnostic message.  Although this behaviour may be somewhat confusing, it is unlikely that anybody actually depends on this be‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 909 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609077, "o", "       haviour.  If the leaf optimisation has been turned off with \u001b[1m-noleaf\u001b[22m, the directory entry will always be  examined  and  the  diagnostic\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 910 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       message  will  be issued where it is appropriate.  Symbolic links cannot be used to create filesystem cycles as such, but if the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mop‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 911 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609154, "o", "       tion or the \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22moption is in use, a diagnostic message is issued when \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mencounters a loop of symbolic links.  As with loops con‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 912 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       taining hard links, the leaf optimisation will often mean that \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mknows that it doesn't need to call \u001b[4mstat()\u001b[24m or \u001b[4mchdir()\u001b[24m  on  the  sym‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 913 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       bolic link, so this diagnostic is frequently not necessary.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 914 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609212, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 915 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22moption is supported for compatibility with various BSD systems, but you should use the POSIX-compliant option \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22minstead.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 916 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 917 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.609267, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609323, "o", "       The \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22menvironment variable does not affect the behaviour of the \u001b[1m-regex \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-iregex \u001b[22mtests because those tests aren't speci‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 918 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       fied in the POSIX standard.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 919 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 920 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609363, "o", "\u001b[1mENVIRONMENT VARIABLES\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 921 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       LANG   Provides a default value for the internationalization variables that are unset or null.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 922 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 923 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609378, "o", "       LC_ALL If set to a non-empty string value, override the values of all the other internationalization variables.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 924 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 925 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       LC_COLLATE\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 926 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.609435, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The POSIX standard specifies that this variable affects the pattern matching to be used for the \u001b[1m-name \u001b[22moption.  GNU find uses the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 927 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mfnmatch\u001b[22m(3) library function, and so support for \u001b[1mLC_COLLATE \u001b[22mdepends on the system library.  This variable also affects the inter‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 928 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              pretation  of  the  response to \u001b[1m-ok\u001b[22m; while the \u001b[1mLC_MESSAGES \u001b[22mvariable selects the actual pattern used to interpret the response to\u001b[m\r\n"]
[2006.60948, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609524, "o", "              \u001b[1m-ok\u001b[22m, the interpretation of any bracket expressions in the pattern will be affected by \u001b[1mLC_COLLATE\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 930 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 931 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       LC_CTYPE\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 932 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              This variable affects the treatment of character classes used in regular expressions and also with the \u001b[1m-name \u001b[22mtest, if  the  sys‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 933 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.609539, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tem's  \u001b[1mfnmatch\u001b[22m(3) library function supports this.  This variable also affects the interpretation of any character classes in the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 934 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              regular expressions used to interpret the response to the prompt issued by \u001b[1m-ok\u001b[22m.  The \u001b[1mLC_CTYPE \u001b[22menvironment variable will also af‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 935 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.60959, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              fect which characters are considered to be unprintable when filenames are printed; see the section UNUSUAL FILENAMES.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 936 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 937 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       LC_MESSAGES\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 938 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609628, "o", "              Determines the locale to be used for internationalised messages.  If the \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22menvironment variable is set, this  also\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 939 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              determines the interpretation of the response to the prompt made by the \u001b[1m-ok \u001b[22maction.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 940 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609663, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 941 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609681, "o", "       NLSPATH\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 942 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Determines the location of the internationalisation message catalogues.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 943 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 944 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609736, "o", "       PATH   Affects the directories which are searched to find the executables invoked by \u001b[1m-exec\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-execdir\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-ok \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-okdir\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 945 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 946 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       POSIXLY_CORRECT\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 947 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60977, "o", "              Determines  the  block size used by \u001b[1m-ls \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-fls\u001b[22m.  If \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22mis set, blocks are units of 512 bytes.  Otherwise they are\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 948 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60981, "o", "              units of 1024 bytes.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 949 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 950 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Setting this variable also turns off warning messages (that is, implies \u001b[1m-nowarn\u001b[22m) by default, because POSIX requires  that  apart\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 951 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.609852, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              from the output for \u001b[1m-ok\u001b[22m, all messages printed on stderr are diagnostics and must result in a non-zero exit status.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 952 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 953 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609892, "o", "              When  \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT  \u001b[22mis  not  set,  \u001b[1m-perm  \u001b[4m\u001b[22m+zzz\u001b[24m  is  treated  just like \u001b[1m-perm \u001b[4m\u001b[22m/zzz\u001b[24m if \u001b[4m+zzz\u001b[24m is not a valid symbolic mode.  When\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 954 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22mis set, such constructs are treated as an error.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 955 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 956 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.60993, "o", "              When \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22mis set, the response to the prompt made by the \u001b[1m-ok \u001b[22maction is interpreted according to the system's  message\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 957 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              catalogue, as opposed to according to \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m's own message translations.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 958 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609964, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 959 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       TZ     Affects the time zone used for some of the time-related format directives of \u001b[1m-printf \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-fprintf\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 960 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 961 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.609995, "o", "\u001b[1mEXAMPLES\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 962 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mSimple `find|xargs` approach\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 963 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610037, "o", "       •      Find files named \u001b[4mcore\u001b[24m in or below the directory \u001b[4m/tmp\u001b[24m and delete them.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 964 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 965 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610075, "o", "                  \u001b[1m$ find /tmp -name core -type f -print | xargs /bin/rm -f\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 966 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 967 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Note that this will work incorrectly if there are any filenames containing newlines, single or double quotes, or spaces.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 968 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610117, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 969 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mSafer `find -print0 | xargs -0` approach\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 970 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Find  files named \u001b[4mcore\u001b[24m in or below the directory \u001b[4m/tmp\u001b[24m and delete them, processing filenames in such a way that file or directory\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 971 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610131, "o", "              names containing single or double quotes, spaces or newlines are correctly handled.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 972 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 973 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find /tmp -name core -type f -print0 | xargs -0 /bin/rm -f\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 974 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.610178, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 975 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The \u001b[1m-name \u001b[22mtest comes before the \u001b[1m-type \u001b[22mtest in order to avoid having to call \u001b[1mstat\u001b[22m(2) on every file.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 976 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 977 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610223, "o", "       Note that there is still a race between the time \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mtraverses the hierarchy printing the matching filenames, and the time the process\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 978 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       executed by \u001b[1mxargs \u001b[22mworks with that file.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 979 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 980 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.610256, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mProcessing arbitrary starting points\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 981 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.610295, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Given that another program \u001b[4mproggy\u001b[24m pre-filters and creates a huge NUL-separated list of files, process those as starting  points,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 982 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610311, "o", "              and find all regular, empty files among them:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 983 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 984 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ proggy | find -files0-from - -maxdepth 0 -type f -empty\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 985 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610367, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 986 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610407, "o", "              The  use  of  \u001b[1m`-files0-from -`  \u001b[22mmeans  to  read  the  names of the starting points from \u001b[4mstandard\u001b[24m \u001b[4minput\u001b[24m, i.e., from the pipe; and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 987 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1m-maxdepth 0 \u001b[22mensures that only explicitly those entries are examined without recursing into directories (in the case one  of  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 988 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              starting points is one).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 989 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 990 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610437, "o", "   \u001b[1mExecuting a command for each file\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 991 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Run \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m on every file in or below the current directory.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 992 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 993 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610471, "o", "                  \u001b[1m$ find . -type f -exec file '{}' \\;\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 994 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 995 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610502, "o", "              Notice  that the braces are enclosed in single quote marks to protect them from interpretation as shell script punctuation.  The\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 996 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              semicolon is similarly protected by the use of a backslash, though single quotes could have been used in that case also.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 997 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610538, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 998 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       In many cases, one might prefer the \u001b[1m`-exec ... +` \u001b[22mor better the \u001b[1m`-execdir ... +` \u001b[22msyntax for performance and security reasons.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 999 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.610577, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1000 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mTraversing the filesystem just once - for 2 different actions\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1001 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610614, "o", "       •      Traverse the filesystem just once,  listing  set-user-ID  files  and  directories  into  \u001b[4m/root/suid.txt\u001b[24m  and  large  files  into\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1002 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[4m/root/big.txt\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1003 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1004 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.610661, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find / \\\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1005 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                      \u001b[1m\\( -perm -4000 -fprintf /root/suid.txt '%#m %u %p\\n' \\) , \\\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1006 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.6107, "o", "                      \u001b[1m\\( -size +100M -fprintf /root/big.txt '%-10s %p\\n' \\)\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1007 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1008 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              This  example uses the line-continuation character '\\' on the first two lines to instruct the shell to continue reading the com‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1009 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610743, "o", "              mand on the next line.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1010 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1011 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mSearching files by age\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1012 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610755, "o", "       •      Search for files in your home directory which have been modified in the last twenty-four hours.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1013 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1014 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find $HOME -mtime 0\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1015 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610811, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1016 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610849, "o", "              This command works this way because the time since each file was last modified is divided by 24 hours and any remainder is  dis‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1017 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              carded.  That means that to match \u001b[1m-mtime 0\u001b[22m, a file will have to have a modification in the past which is less than 24 hours ago.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1018 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1019 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610888, "o", "   \u001b[1mSearching files by permissions\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1020 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Search for files which are executable but not readable.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1021 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1022 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610926, "o", "                  \u001b[1m$ find /sbin /usr/sbin -executable \\! -readable -print\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1023 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1024 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.610963, "o", "       •      Search  for  files which have read and write permission for their owner, and group, but which other users can read but not write\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1025 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              to.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1026 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1027 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611001, "o", "                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm 664\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1028 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1029 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Files which meet these criteria but have other permissions bits set (for example if someone can execute the file)  will  not  be\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1030 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611034, "o", "              matched.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1031 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1032 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611073, "o", "       •      Search  for files which have read and write permission for their owner and group, and which other users can read, without regard\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1033 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              to the presence of any extra permission bits (for example the executable bit).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1034 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1035 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.611108, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm -664\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1036 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1037 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              This will match a file which has mode \u001b[4m0777\u001b[24m, for example.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1038 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1039 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611144, "o", "       •      Search for files which are writable by somebody (their owner, or their group, or anybody else).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1040 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1041 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611174, "o", "                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm /222\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1042 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1043 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Search for files which are writable by either their owner or their group.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1044 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.611206, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1045 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.611246, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm /220\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1046 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm /u+w,g+w\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1047 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611279, "o", "                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm /u=w,g=w\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1048 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1049 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611296, "o", "              All three of these commands do the same thing, but the first one uses the octal representation of the file mode, and  the  other\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1050 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              two use the symbolic form.  The files don't have to be writable by both the owner and group to be matched; either will do.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1051 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1052 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.611348, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Search for files which are writable by both their owner and their group.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1053 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1054 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm -220\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1055 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611383, "o", "                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm -g+w,u+w\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1056 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611415, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1057 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Both these commands do the same thing.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1058 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1059 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.611449, "o", "       •      A more elaborate search on permissions.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1060 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1061 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm -444 -perm /222 \\! -perm /111\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find . -perm -a+r -perm /a+w \\! -perm /a+x\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1063 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.612441, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1064 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              These two commands both search for files that are readable for everybody (\u001b[1m-perm -444 \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-perm -a+r\u001b[22m), have at least one write bit\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1065 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              set (\u001b[1m-perm /222 \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-perm /a+w\u001b[22m) but are not executable for anybody (\u001b[1m! -perm /111 \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m! -perm /a+x \u001b[22mrespectively).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1066 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1067 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mPruning - omitting files and subdirectories\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1068 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Copy  the  contents of \u001b[4m/source-dir\u001b[24m to \u001b[4m/dest-dir\u001b[24m, but omit files and directories named \u001b[4m.snapshot\u001b[24m (and anything in them).  It also\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1069 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              omits files or directories whose name ends in `~', but not their contents.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1070 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1071 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ cd /source-dir\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1072 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find . -name .snapshot -prune -o \\( \\! -name '*~' -print0 \\) \\\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1073 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                      \u001b[1m| cpio -pmd0 /dest-dir\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1074 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1075 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The construct \u001b[1m-prune -o \\( ... -print0 \\) \u001b[22mis quite common.  The idea here is that the expression before  \u001b[1m-prune  \u001b[22mmatches  things\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1076 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              which are to be pruned.  However, the \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22maction itself returns true, so the following \u001b[1m-o \u001b[22mensures that the right hand side is\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1077 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              evaluated  only  for  those directories which didn't get pruned (the contents of the pruned directories are not even visited, so\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1078 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              their contents are irrelevant).  The expression on the right hand side of the \u001b[1m-o \u001b[22mis in parentheses only for clarity.  It  empha‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1079 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              sises  that  the  \u001b[1m-print0 \u001b[22maction takes place only for things that didn't have \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mapplied to them.  Because the default `and'\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1080 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              condition between tests binds more tightly than \u001b[1m-o\u001b[22m, this is the default anyway, but the parentheses help to show what  is  going\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1081 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              on.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1082 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1083 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Given  the  following directory of projects and their associated SCM administrative directories, perform an efficient search for\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1084 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the projects' roots:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1085 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1086 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find repo/ \\\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1087 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                      \u001b[1m\\( -exec test -d '{}/.svn' \\; \\\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1088 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                      \u001b[1m-or -exec test -d '{}/.git' \\; \\\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1089 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                      \u001b[1m-or -exec test -d '{}/CVS' \\; \\\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1090 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                      \u001b[1m\\) -print -prune\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1091 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1092 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Sample output:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1093 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1094 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1mrepo/project1/CVS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1095 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1mrepo/gnu/project2/.svn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1096 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1mrepo/gnu/project3/.svn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1097 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1mrepo/gnu/project3/src/.svn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1098 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1mrepo/project4/.git\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1099 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1100 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              In this example, \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mprevents unnecessary descent into directories that have already been discovered (for example we  do  not\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1101 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              search \u001b[4mproject3/src\u001b[24m because we already found \u001b[4mproject3/.svn\u001b[24m), but ensures sibling directories (\u001b[4mproject2\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mproject3\u001b[24m) are found.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1102 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1103 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mOther useful examples\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1104 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Search for several file types.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1105 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1106 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find /tmp -type f,d,l\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1107 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1108 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Search  for  files, directories, and symbolic links in the directory \u001b[4m/tmp\u001b[24m passing these types as a comma-separated list (GNU ex‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1109 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tension), which is otherwise equivalent to the longer, yet more portable:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1110 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1111 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find /tmp \\( -type f -o -type d -o -type l \\)\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1112 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1113 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Search for files with the particular name \u001b[4mneedle\u001b[24m and stop immediately when we find the first one.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1114 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1115 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find / -name needle -print -quit\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1116 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1117 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       •      Demonstrate the interpretation of the \u001b[1m%f \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m%h \u001b[22mformat directives of the \u001b[1m-printf \u001b[22maction for some corner-cases.  Here is an exam‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1118 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ple including some output.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1119 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1120 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m$ find . .. / /tmp /tmp/TRACE compile compile/64/tests/find -maxdepth 0 -printf '[%h][%f]\\n'\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1121 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m[.][.]\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1122 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m[.][..]\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1123 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m[][/]\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1124 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m[][tmp]\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1125 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m[/tmp][TRACE]\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1126 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m[.][compile]\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1127 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  \u001b[1m[compile/64/tests][find]\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1128 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1129 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[1mEXIT STATUS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1130 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mexits with status 0 if all files are processed successfully, greater than 0 if errors occur.  This is deliberately  a  very  broad\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1131 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.612502, "o", "       description, but if the return value is non-zero, you should not rely on the correctness of the results of \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1132 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.612538, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1133 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       When some error occurs, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mmay stop immediately, without completing all the actions specified.  For example, some starting points may\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1134 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       not have been examined or some pending program invocations for \u001b[1m-exec ... {} + \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-execdir ... {} + \u001b[22mmay not have been performed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1135 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1136 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[1mHISTORY\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1137 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.612575, "o", "       A \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mprogram appeared in Version 5 Unix as part of the Programmer's Workbench project and was written by Dick Haight.  Doug McIlroy's\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1138 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.612609, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4mA\u001b[24m  \u001b[4mResearch\u001b[24m  \u001b[4mUNIX\u001b[24m  \u001b[4mReader:\u001b[24m \u001b[4mAnnotated\u001b[24m \u001b[4mExcerpts\u001b[24m \u001b[4mfrom\u001b[24m \u001b[4mthe\u001b[24m \u001b[4mProgrammer’s\u001b[24m \u001b[4mManual,\u001b[24m \u001b[4m1971-1986\u001b[24m provides some additional details; you can read it\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1139 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.612643, "o", "       on-line at <https://www.cs.dartmouth.edu/~doug/reader.pdf>.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1140 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1141 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.612696, "o", "       GNU \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwas originally written by Eric Decker, with enhancements by David MacKenzie, Jay Plett, and  Tim  Wood.   The  idea  for  \u001b[1mfind\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1142 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-print0 \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mxargs -0 \u001b[22mcame from Dan Bernstein.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1143 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1144 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.612726, "o", "\u001b[1mCOMPATIBILITY\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1145 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       As  of findutils-4.2.2, shell metacharacters (`*', `?' or `[]' for example) used in filename patterns match a leading `.', because IEEE\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1146 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       POSIX interpretation 126 requires this.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1147 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1148 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.612789, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       As of findutils-4.3.3, \u001b[1m-perm /000 \u001b[22mnow matches all files instead of none.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1149 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.612833, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1150 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Nanosecond-resolution timestamps were implemented in findutils-4.3.3.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1151 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1152 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       As of findutils-4.3.11, the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction sets \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m's exit status to a nonzero value when it fails.  However, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwill not exit imme‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1153 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.612851, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       diately.  Previously, \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m's exit status was unaffected by the failure of \u001b[1m-delete\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1154 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       Feature                Added in   Also occurs in\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1155 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
