[2006.613318, "o", "       The syntax \u001b[1m-perm +MODE \u001b[22mwas removed in findutils-4.5.12, in favour of \u001b[1m-perm /MODE\u001b[22m.  The \u001b[1m+MODE \u001b[22msyntax had been  deprecated  since  findu‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1183 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       tils-4.2.21 which was released in 2005.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1184 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.613366, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1185 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[1mNON-BUGS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1186 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mOperator precedence surprises\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1187 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.6134, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The  command  \u001b[1mfind . -name afile -o -name bfile -print \u001b[22mwill never print \u001b[4mafile\u001b[24m because this is actually equivalent to \u001b[1mfind . -name afile\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1188 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m-o \\( -name bfile -a -print \\)\u001b[22m.  Remember that the precedence of \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mis higher than that of \u001b[1m-o \u001b[22mand when there is no  operator  specified\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1189 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.613443, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       between tests, \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mis assumed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1190 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1191 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.613458, "o", "   \u001b[1m“paths must precede expression” error message\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1192 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m$ find . -name *.c -print\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1193 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       find: paths must precede expression\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1194 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2006.613507, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       find: possible unquoted pattern after predicate `-name'?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1195 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1196 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       This  happens when the shell could expand the pattern \u001b[4m*.c\u001b[24m to more than one file name existing in the current directory, and passing the\u001b[m\r\n"]
[2006.613542, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.613577, "o", "       resulting file names in the command line to \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mlike this:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1198 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1mfind . -name frcode.c locate.c word_io.c -print\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1199 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.61361, "o", "       That command is of course not going to work, because the \u001b[1m-name \u001b[22mpredicate allows exactly only one pattern as argument.  Instead of doing\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1200 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       things this way, you should enclose the pattern in quotes or escape the wildcard, thus allowing \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mto use the pattern with the  wild‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1201 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.61365, "o", "       card during the search for file name matching instead of file names expanded by the parent shell:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1202 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.613689, "o", "       \u001b[1m$ find . -name '*.c' -print\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1203 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[1m$ find . -name \\*.c -print\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1204 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1205 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.613735, "o", "\u001b[1mBUGS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1206 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       There are security problems inherent in the behaviour that the POSIX standard specifies for \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m, which therefore cannot be fixed.  For\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1207 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2006.613777, "o", "       example, the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22maction is inherently insecure, and \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[22mshould be used instead.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1208 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1209 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       The environment variable \u001b[1mLC_COLLATE \u001b[22mhas no effect on the \u001b[1m-ok \u001b[22maction.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 1210 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
