[2013.904898, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM              ror output, respectively.  The output file is always created, even if the predicate is never matched.  See the \u001b[1mUNUSUAL FILENAMES\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 592/1271 56% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              truncated.  The file names \u001b[4m/dev/stdout\u001b[24m and \u001b[4m/dev/stderr\u001b[24m are handled specially; they refer to the standard output and standard er‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 591/1271 56% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K"]
[2013.905077, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM              True; print the full file name into file \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m.  If \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m does not exist when \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mis run, it is created; if it does exist, it  is\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 590/1271 56% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2013.934185, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -fprint \u001b[4mfile\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 589/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 588/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              the \u001b[1mUNUSUAL FILENAMES \u001b[22msection for information about how unusual characters in filenames are handled.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 587/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              True;  like \u001b[1m-ls \u001b[22mbut write to \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m like \u001b[1m-fprint\u001b[22m.  The output file is always created, even if the predicate is never matched.  See\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 586/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.092388, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -fls \u001b[4mfile\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 585/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 584/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[4mmand\u001b[24m \u001b[1m{} + \u001b[22malways returns true, while \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcommand\u001b[24m \u001b[1m{} ; \u001b[22mreturns true only if \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m returns 0.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 583/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.120833, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              mands may not be run at all.  The result of the action depends on whether the \u001b[1m+ \u001b[22mor the \u001b[1m; \u001b[22mvariant is  being  used;  \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcom‐\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 582/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              returns  a  non-zero exit status.  If \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mencounters an error, this can sometimes cause an immediate exit, so some pending com‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 581/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.128388, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              which are not absolute directory names.  If any invocation with the `+' form returns a non-zero value as exit status, then  \u001b[1mfind\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 580/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              ately-named  file  in a directory in which you will run \u001b[1m-execdir\u001b[22m.  The same applies to having entries in \u001b[1mPATH \u001b[22mwhich are empty or\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 579/1271 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.17204, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[1mPATH \u001b[22menvironment variable does not reference `.'; otherwise, an attacker can run any commands they like by leaving an  appropri‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 578/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              cation  of  \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m will only list files that exist in the same subdirectory.  If you use this option, you must ensure that your\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 577/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22maction, the `+' form of \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[22mwill build a command line to process more than one matched file, but any given  invo‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 576/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              secure  method for invoking commands, as it avoids race conditions during resolution of the paths to the matched files.  As with\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 575/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.17958, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              tory in which you started \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.  As with -exec, the {} should be quoted if find is being invoked from a shell.  This a much more\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 574/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              Like \u001b[1m-exec\u001b[22m, but the specified command is run from the subdirectory containing the matched file, which is not normally the direc‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 573/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -execdir \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m {} +\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 572/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.196441, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 571/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -execdir \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m ;\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 570/1271 54% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 569/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K"]
[2015.196614, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[4mmand\u001b[24m \u001b[1m... {} + -quit \u001b[22mmay not result in \u001b[4mmy-command\u001b[24m actually being run.  This variant of \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22malways returns true.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 568/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.204754, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              ror, this can sometimes cause an immediate exit, so some pending commands may not be run at all.  For this reason  \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[4m\u001b[22mmy-com‐\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 567/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              with  the `+' form returns a non-zero value as exit status, then \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mreturns a non-zero exit status.  If \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mencounters an er‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 566/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              quoted to protect it from interpretation by the shell.  The command is executed in the starting directory.   If  any  invocation\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 565/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              lowed  within  the  command,  and  it must appear at the end, immediately before the `+'; it needs to be escaped (with a `\\') or\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 564/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.220558, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              files.  The command line is built in much the same way that \u001b[1mxargs \u001b[22mbuilds its command lines.  Only one instance of  `{}'  is  al‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 563/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K"]
[2015.220714, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM              each  selected file name at the end; the total number of invocations of the command will be much less than the number of matched\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 562/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              This variant of the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22maction runs the specified command on the selected files, but the command line is  built  by  appending\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 561/1271 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K"]
[2015.221407, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM       -exec \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m {} +\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 560/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 559/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.236682, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              the \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[22moption instead.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 558/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              executed in the starting directory.  There are unavoidable security problems surrounding use of the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22maction; you should use\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 557/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.236802, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              section  for  examples of the use of the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22moption.  The specified command is run once for each matched file.  The command is\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 556/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K"]
[2015.237249, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM              constructions might need to be escaped (with a `\\') or quoted to protect them from expansion by the  shell.   See  the  \u001b[1mEXAMPLES\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 555/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              it  occurs in the arguments to the command, not just in arguments where it is alone, as in some versions of \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.  Both of these\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 554/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              an argument consisting of `;' is encountered.  The string `{}' is replaced by the current file name being  processed  everywhere\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 553/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              Execute  \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m;  true if 0 status is returned.  All following arguments to \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mare taken to be arguments to the command until\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 552/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -exec \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m ;\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 551/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 550/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.253719, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              return code of the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction will be true.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 549/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.253824, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              peared since the parent directory was read: it will not output an error diagnostic, not change the exit code to nonzero, and the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 548/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.286687, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              Together with the \u001b[1m-ignore_readdir_race \u001b[22moption, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwill ignore errors of the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction in the case  the  file  has  disap‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 547/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 546/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.311415, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              The \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction will fail to remove a directory unless it is empty.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 545/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 544/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.328528, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              surprising results, it is usually best to remember to use \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22mexplicitly during those earlier test runs.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 543/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K"]
[2015.328668, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM              Often, the user might want to test a \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mcommand line with \u001b[1m-print \u001b[22mprior to adding \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22mfor the actual removal run.  To avoid\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 542/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.354618, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 541/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K"]
[2015.35477, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM              effective, the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction cannot usefully be combined with \u001b[1m-prune\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 540/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.396502, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              The  use of the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction on the command line automatically turns on the \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22moption.  As in turn \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22mmakes \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22min‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 539/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 538/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              delete everything below the starting points you specified.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 537/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.444146, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[1mWarning\u001b[22m: Don't forget that \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mevaluates the command line as an expression, so putting \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22mfirst  will  make  \u001b[1mfind  \u001b[22mtry  to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 536/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 535/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.45236, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              tus will be nonzero (when it eventually exits).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 534/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              Delete  files or directories; true if removal succeeded.  If the removal failed, an error message is issued and \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m's exit sta‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 533/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.652893, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -delete\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 532/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM   \u001b[1mACTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 531/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.661626, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 530/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              (SELinux only) Security context of the file matches glob \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 529/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.731563, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -context \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 528/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 527/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              not exist or the link points to itself) then \u001b[1m-xtype \u001b[22mwill behave the same as \u001b[1m-type\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 526/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.796202, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              \u001b[1m-xtype \u001b[22mchecks the type of the file that \u001b[1m-type \u001b[22mdoes not check.  If a symbolic link is broken (because the thing it points to does\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 525/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              file is a link to a file of type \u001b[4mc\u001b[24m; if the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption has been given, true if \u001b[4mc\u001b[24m is `l'.  In  other  words,  for  symbolic  links,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 524/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.821425, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              The  same  as  \u001b[1m-type  \u001b[22munless the file is a symbolic link.  For symbolic links: if the \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22moption was specified, true if the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 523/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -xtype \u001b[4mc\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 522/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2015.997499, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 521/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              UID mapping information held on the server.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 520/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2016.133827, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              do UID mapping (or root-squashing), since many systems implement \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) in the client's kernel and so cannot make use of  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 519/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              facts which the \u001b[1m-perm \u001b[22mtest ignores.  This test makes use of the \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) system call, and so can be fooled by NFS servers which\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 518/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2016.212557, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              Matches  files which are writable by the current user.  This takes into account access control lists and other permissions arte‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 517/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -writable\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 516/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2016.283183, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 515/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              See -path.  This alternative is less portable than \u001b[1m-path\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 514/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -wholename \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 513/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 512/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              File is owned by user \u001b[4muname\u001b[24m (numeric user ID allowed).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 511/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2016.304191, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -user \u001b[4muname\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 510/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 509/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2016.304494, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              File was last accessed less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m days after its status was last changed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 508/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -used \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 507/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2016.337221, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 506/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       -uid \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m File's numeric user ID is less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 505/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2016.364687, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 504/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              sion).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 503/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM              To search for more than one type at once, you can supply the combined list of type letters separated by a comma `,' (GNU  exten‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 502/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
