[2033.313328, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[4m-n\u001b[24m     for less than \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 282/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 281/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2033.320877, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[4m+n\u001b[24m     for greater than \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 280/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 279/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2033.907928, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       A numeric argument \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m can be specified to tests (like \u001b[1m-amin\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-mtime\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-gid\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-inum\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-links\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-size\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-uid \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-used\u001b[22m) as\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 278/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 277/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2034.001385, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       nonzero status.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 276/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       ence  file  cannot  be  examined (for example, the \u001b[1mstat\u001b[22m(2) system call fails for it), an error message is issued, and \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mexits with a\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 275/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2034.074642, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       and \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22mand any previous \u001b[1m-follow\u001b[22m, but the reference file is only examined once, at the time the command line is parsed.  If  the  refer‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 274/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM       specified on the command line.  When these tests are used, the interpretation of the reference file is determined by the options \u001b[1m-H\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-L\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 273/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K"]
[2034.07481, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM       Some  tests,  for  example  \u001b[1m-newerXY  \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-samefile\u001b[22m, allow comparison between the file currently being examined and some reference file\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 272/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2034.153803, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM   \u001b[1mTESTS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 271/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KA\bA\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[41;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 270/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2035.130294, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File's status was last changed less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m*24 hours ago.  See the comments for \u001b[1m-atime  \u001b[22mto  understand  how\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 271/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2035.245447, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              rounding affects the interpretation of file status change times.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 272/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 273/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -empty File is empty and is either a regular file or a directory.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 274/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2035.309888, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 275/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -executable\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 276/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2035.431245, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Matches  files  which are executable and directories which are searchable (in a file name resolution sense) by the current user.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 277/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2035.431422, "o", "              This takes into account access control lists and other permissions artefacts which the \u001b[1m-perm \u001b[22mtest ignores.  This test makes  use\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 278/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2036.177018, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              of  the  \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) system call, and so can be fooled by NFS servers which do UID mapping (or root-squashing), since many systems\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 279/1271 29% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              implement \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) in the client's kernel and so cannot make use of the UID mapping information held on  the  server.   Because\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 280/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.668544, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.668606, "o", "              this  test  is based only on the result of the \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) system call, there is no guarantee that a file for which this test suc‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 281/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ceeds can actually be executed.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 282/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.668941, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 283/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -false Always false.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 284/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 285/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.705541, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.705649, "o", "       -fstype \u001b[4mtype\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 286/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.706142, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File is on a filesystem of type \u001b[4mtype\u001b[24m.  The valid filesystem types vary among different versions of Unix; an incomplete  list  of\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 287/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              filesystem types that are accepted on some version of Unix or another is: ufs, 4.2, 4.3, nfs, tmp, mfs, S51K, S52K.  You can use\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 288/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1m-printf \u001b[22mwith the %F directive to see the types of your filesystems.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 289/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.706218, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 290/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -gid \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m File's numeric group ID is less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 291/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 292/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.706456, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -group \u001b[4mgname\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 293/1271 30% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File belongs to group \u001b[4mgname\u001b[24m (numeric group ID allowed).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 294/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.706522, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 295/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.70695, "o", "       -ilname \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 296/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.707001, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Like  \u001b[1m-lname\u001b[22m,  but  the match is case insensitive.  If the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption or the \u001b[1m-follow \u001b[22moption is in effect, this test returns false\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 297/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              unless the symbolic link is broken.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 298/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 299/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -iname \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 300/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Like \u001b[1m-name\u001b[22m, but the match is case insensitive.  For example, the patterns `fo*' and `F??' match the  file  names  `Foo',  `FOO',\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 301/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.707077, "o", "              `foo', `fOo', etc.  The pattern `*foo*` will also match a file called '.foobar'.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 302/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.707145, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 303/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.707185, "o", "       -inum \u001b[4mn\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 304/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.70725, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.707294, "o", "              File has inode number smaller than, greater than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m.  It is normally easier to use the \u001b[1m-samefile \u001b[22mtest instead.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 305/1271 31% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
