[2047.725816, "o", "              rounding affects the interpretation of file modification times.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 328/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 329/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.725889, "o", "       -name \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 330/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Base  of  file name (the path with the leading directories removed) matches shell pattern \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.  Because the leading directo‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 331/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.732712, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ries of the file names are removed, the \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m should not include a slash, because `-name a/b' will never match  anything  (and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 332/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              you  probably  want to use \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22minstead).  An exception to this is when using only a slash as \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m (`-name /'), because that\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 333/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              is a valid string for matching the root directory \"/\" (because the base name of \"/\" is \"/\").  A warning is issued if you try  to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 334/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.73281, "o", "              pass  a  pattern containing a - but not consisting solely of one - slash, unless the environment variable \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22mis set\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 335/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              or the option \u001b[1m-nowarn \u001b[22mis used.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 336/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 337/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.754033, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.754174, "o", "              To ignore a directory and the files under it, use \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mrather than checking every file in the tree; see an example in the  de‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 338/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              scription  of  that  action.  Braces are not recognised as being special, despite the fact that some shells including Bash imbue\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 339/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              braces with a special meaning in shell patterns.  The filename matching is performed with the  use  of  the  \u001b[1mfnmatch\u001b[22m(3)  library\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 340/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              function.  Don't forget to enclose the pattern in quotes in order to protect it from expansion by the shell.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 341/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.754254, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 342/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -newer \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 343/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.754638, "o", "              Time  of  the last data modification of the current file is more recent than that of the last data modification of the \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 344/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              file.  If \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m is a symbolic link and the \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22moption or the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption is in effect, then the time of the last data modifica‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 345/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tion of the file it points to is always used.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 346/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 347/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -newerXY \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 348/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Succeeds if timestamp \u001b[4mX\u001b[24m of the file being considered is newer than timestamp \u001b[4mY\u001b[24m of the file \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m.  The letters \u001b[4mX\u001b[24m and  \u001b[4mY\u001b[24m  can\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 349/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.754758, "o", "              be any of the following letters:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 350/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.771513, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 351/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              a   The access time of the file \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 352/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              B   The birth time of the file \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 353/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.771687, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              c   The inode status change time of \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 354/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              m   The modification time of the file \u001b[4mreference\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 355/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.787713, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              t   \u001b[4mreference\u001b[24m is interpreted directly as a time\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 356/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 357/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.804811, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Some  combinations are invalid; for example, it is invalid for \u001b[4mX\u001b[24m to be \u001b[4mt\u001b[24m.  Some combinations are not implemented on all systems;\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 358/1271 35% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2047.804995, "o", "              for example \u001b[4mB\u001b[24m is not supported on all systems.  If an invalid or unsupported combination of \u001b[4mXY\u001b[24m is specified, a fatal  error  re‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 359/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.820657, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              sults.   Time specifications are interpreted as for the argument to the \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22moption of GNU \u001b[1mdate\u001b[22m.  If you try to use the birth time\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 360/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              of a reference file, and the birth time cannot be determined, a fatal error message results.  If you specify a test which refers\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 361/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2047.838149, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              to the birth time of files being examined, this test will fail for any files where the birth time is unknown.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 362/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 363/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
