[2070.686658, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -name \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 330/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Base  of  file name (the path with the leading directories removed) matches shell pattern \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.  Because the leading directo‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 331/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2070.703352, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ries of the file names are removed, the \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m should not include a slash, because `-name a/b' will never match  anything  (and\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 332/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2070.703539, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              you  probably  want to use \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22minstead).  An exception to this is when using only a slash as \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m (`-name /'), because that\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 333/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              is a valid string for matching the root directory \"/\" (because the base name of \"/\" is \"/\").  A warning is issued if you try  to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 334/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2070.70383, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              pass  a  pattern containing a - but not consisting solely of one - slash, unless the environment variable \u001b[1mPOSIXLY_CORRECT \u001b[22mis set\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 335/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2070.736447, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              or the option \u001b[1m-nowarn \u001b[22mis used.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 336/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2070.736508, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 337/1271 33% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2070.736609, "o", "              To ignore a directory and the files under it, use \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mrather than checking every file in the tree; see an example in the  de‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 338/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              scription  of  that  action.  Braces are not recognised as being special, despite the fact that some shells including Bash imbue\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 339/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2070.76452, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2070.764597, "o", "              braces with a special meaning in shell patterns.  The filename matching is performed with the  use  of  the  \u001b[1mfnmatch\u001b[22m(3)  library\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 340/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              function.  Don't forget to enclose the pattern in quotes in order to protect it from expansion by the shell.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 341/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2070.764626, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 342/1271 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
