[2071.475547, "o", "              No user corresponds to file's numeric user ID.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 368/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 369/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -path \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 370/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File name matches shell pattern \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.  The metacharacters do not treat `/' or `.' specially; so, for example,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 371/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.476027, "o", "                  find . -path \"./sr*sc\"\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 372/1271 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              will print an entry for a directory called \u001b[4m./src/misc\u001b[24m (if one exists).  To ignore a whole directory tree, use \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mrather than\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 373/1271 37% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              checking every file in the tree.  Note that the pattern match test applies to the whole file name,  starting  from  one  of  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 374/1271 37% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              start  points named on the command line.  It would only make sense to use an absolute path name here if the relevant start point\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 375/1271 37% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              is also an absolute path.  This means that this command will never match anything:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 376/1271 37% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  find bar -path /foo/bar/myfile -print\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 377/1271 37% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Find compares the \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22margument with the concatenation of a directory name and the base name of the file it's examining.  Since\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 378/1271 37% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.476297, "o", "              the concatenation will never end with a slash, \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22marguments ending in a slash will match  nothing  (except  perhaps  a  start\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 379/1271 37% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              point  specified  on the command line).  The predicate \u001b[1m-path \u001b[22mis also supported by HP-UX \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mand is part of the POSIX 2008 stan‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 380/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.476534, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              dard.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 381/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 382/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -perm \u001b[4mmode\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 383/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File's permission bits are exactly \u001b[4mmode\u001b[24m (octal or symbolic).  Since an exact match is required, if you want to use this form for\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 384/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              symbolic modes, you may have to specify a rather complex mode string.  For example `-perm g=w' will only match files which  have\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 385/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.476627, "o", "              mode  0020 (that is, ones for which group write permission is the only permission set).  It is more likely that you will want to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 386/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              use the `/' or `-' forms, for example `-perm -g=w', which matches any file with group write permission.  See the  \u001b[1mEXAMPLES  \u001b[22msec‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 387/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tion for some illustrative examples.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 388/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.476703, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 389/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -perm -\u001b[4mmode\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 390/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.476877, "o", "              All  of the permission bits \u001b[4mmode\u001b[24m are set for the file.  Symbolic modes are accepted in this form, and this is usually the way in\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 391/1271 38% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.477253, "o", "              which you would want to use them.  You must specify `u', `g' or `o' if you use a symbolic mode.  See the  \u001b[1mEXAMPLES  \u001b[22msection  for\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 392/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              some illustrative examples.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 393/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.47731, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 394/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -perm /\u001b[4mmode\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 395/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Any  of  the permission bits \u001b[4mmode\u001b[24m are set for the file.  Symbolic modes are accepted in this form.  You must specify `u', `g' or\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 396/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `o' if you use a symbolic mode.  See the \u001b[1mEXAMPLES \u001b[22msection for some illustrative examples.  If no permission  bits  in  \u001b[4mmode\u001b[24m  are\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 397/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              set, this test matches any file (the idea here is to be consistent with the behaviour of \u001b[1m-perm -000\u001b[22m).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 398/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 399/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -perm +\u001b[4mmode\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 400/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.477448, "o", "              This is no longer supported (and has been deprecated since 2005).  Use \u001b[1m-perm /\u001b[4m\u001b[22mmode\u001b[24m instead.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 401/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 402/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -readable\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 403/1271 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.481996, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Matches  files which are readable by the current user.  This takes into account access control lists and other permissions arte‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 404/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.482112, "o", "              facts which the \u001b[1m-perm \u001b[22mtest ignores.  This test makes use of the \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) system call, and so can be fooled by NFS servers which\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 405/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              do UID mapping (or root-squashing), since many systems implement \u001b[1maccess\u001b[22m(2) in the client's kernel and so cannot make use of  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 406/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              UID mapping information held on the server.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 407/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.482266, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 408/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -regex \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 409/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File  name  matches  regular expression \u001b[4mpattern\u001b[24m.  This is a match on the whole path, not a search.  For example, to match a file\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 410/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              named \u001b[4m./fubar3,\u001b[24m you can use the regular expression `.*bar.' or `.*b.*3', but not `f.*r3'.  The regular expressions understood by\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 411/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.482291, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.482446, "o", "              \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mare by default Emacs Regular Expressions, but this can be changed with the \u001b[1m-regextype \u001b[22moption.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 412/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 413/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -samefile \u001b[4mname\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 414/1271 40% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File refers to the same inode as \u001b[4mname\u001b[24m.  When \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mis in effect, this can include symbolic links.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 415/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 416/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.482519, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.482703, "o", "       -size \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m[cwbkMG]\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 417/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File uses less than, more than or exactly \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m units of space, rounding up.  The following suffixes can be used:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 418/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 419/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `b'    for 512-byte blocks (this is the default if no suffix is used)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 420/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 421/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `c'    for bytes\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 422/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.482793, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 423/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.50432, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.504911, "o", "              `w'    for two-byte words\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 424/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 425/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `k'    for kibibytes (KiB, units of 1024 bytes)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 426/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 427/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `M'    for mebibytes (MiB, units of 1024 * 1024 = 1048576 bytes)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 428/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 429/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              `G'    for gibibytes (GiB, units of 1024 * 1024 * 1024 = 1073741824 bytes)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 430/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 431/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.505043, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The size is simply the st_size member of the struct stat populated by the lstat (or stat)  system  call,  rounded  up  as  shown\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 432/1271 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.505393, "o", "              above.   In  other  words, it's consistent with the result you get for \u001b[1mls -l\u001b[22m.  Bear in mind that the `%k' and `%b' format speci‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 433/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.505617, "o", "              fiers of \u001b[1m-printf \u001b[22mhandle sparse files differently.  The `b' suffix always denotes 512-byte blocks  and  never  1024-byte  blocks,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 434/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              which is different to the behaviour of \u001b[1m-ls\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 435/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 436/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.50595, "o", "              The  + and - prefixes signify greater than and less than, as usual; i.e., an exact size of \u001b[4mn\u001b[24m units does not match.  Bear in mind\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 437/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              that the size is rounded up to the next unit.  Therefore \u001b[1m-size -1M \u001b[22mis  not  equivalent  to  \u001b[1m-size -1048576c\u001b[22m.   The  former  only\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 438/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              matches empty files, the latter matches files from 0 to 1,048,575 bytes.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 439/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 440/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -true  Always true.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 441/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 442/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -type \u001b[4mc\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 443/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              File is of type \u001b[4mc\u001b[24m:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 444/1271 42% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 445/12