[2071.508018, "o", "              The  same  as  \u001b[1m-type  \u001b[22munless the file is a symbolic link.  For symbolic links: if the \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22moption was specified, true if the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 484/1271 44% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.508087, "o", "              file is a link to a file of type \u001b[4mc\u001b[24m; if the \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22moption has been given, true if \u001b[4mc\u001b[24m is `l'.  In  other  words,  for  symbolic  links,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 485/1271 45% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.50815, "o", "              \u001b[1m-xtype \u001b[22mchecks the type of the file that \u001b[1m-type \u001b[22mdoes not check.  If a symbolic link is broken (because the thing it points to does\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 486/1271 45% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.508215, "o", "              not exist or the link points to itself) then \u001b[1m-xtype \u001b[22mwill behave the same as \u001b[1m-type\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 487/1271 45% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
