[2071.509959, "o", "              \u001b[1mWarning\u001b[22m: Don't forget that \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mevaluates the command line as an expression, so putting \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22mfirst  will  make  \u001b[1mfind  \u001b[22mtry  to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 497/1271 45% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.510127, "o", "              delete everything below the starting points you specified.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 498/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 499/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The  use of the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction on the command line automatically turns on the \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22moption.  As in turn \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22mmakes \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22min‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 500/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              effective, the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction cannot usefully be combined with \u001b[1m-prune\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 501/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 502/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Often, the user might want to test a \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mcommand line with \u001b[1m-print \u001b[22mprior to adding \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22mfor the actual removal run.  To avoid\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 503/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              surprising results, it is usually best to remember to use \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22mexplicitly during those earlier test runs.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 504/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.520391, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.520706, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 505/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction will fail to remove a directory unless it is empty.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 506/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 507/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Together with the \u001b[1m-ignore_readdir_race \u001b[22moption, \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mwill ignore errors of the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction in the case  the  file  has  disap‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 508/1271 46% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.520961, "o", "              peared since the parent directory was read: it will not output an error diagnostic, not change the exit code to nonzero, and the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 509/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              return code of the \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22maction will be true.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 510/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 511/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.521055, "o", "       -exec \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m ;\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 512/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.521151, "o", "              Execute  \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m;  true if 0 status is returned.  All following arguments to \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mare taken to be arguments to the command until\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 513/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              an argument consisting of `;' is encountered.  The string `{}' is replaced by the current file name being  processed  everywhere\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 514/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.521251, "o", "              it  occurs in the arguments to the command, not just in arguments where it is alone, as in some versions of \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.  Both of these\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 515/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.521334, "o", "              constructions might need to be escaped (with a `\\') or quoted to protect them from expansion by the  shell.   See  the  \u001b[1mEXAMPLES\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 516/1271 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              section  for  examples of the use of the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22moption.  The specified command is run once for each matched file.  The command is\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 517/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.521926, "o", "              executed in the starting directory.  There are unavoidable security problems surrounding use of the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22maction; you should use\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 518/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[22moption instead.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 519/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 520/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -exec \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m {} +\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 521/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.522113, "o", "              This variant of the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22maction runs the specified command on the selected files, but the command line is  built  by  appending\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 522/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              each  selected file name at the end; the total number of invocations of the command will be much less than the number of matched\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 523/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              files.  The command line is built in much the same way that \u001b[1mxargs \u001b[22mbuilds its command lines.  Only one instance of  `{}'  is  al‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 524/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              lowed  within  the  command,  and  it must appear at the end, immediately before the `+'; it needs to be escaped (with a `\\') or\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 525/1271 48% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              quoted to protect it from interpretation by the shell.  The command is executed in the starting directory.   If  any  invocation\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 526/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              with  the `+' form returns a non-zero value as exit status, then \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mreturns a non-zero exit status.  If \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mencounters an er‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 527/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ror, this can sometimes cause an immediate exit, so some pending commands may not be run at all.  For this reason  \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[4m\u001b[22mmy-com‐\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 528/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.522187, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[4mmand\u001b[24m \u001b[1m... {} + -quit \u001b[22mmay not result in \u001b[4mmy-command\u001b[24m actually being run.  This variant of \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22malways returns true.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 529/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.522257, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 530/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.522322, "o", "       -execdir \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m ;\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 531/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 532/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.522394, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -execdir \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m {} +\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 533/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.522876, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Like \u001b[1m-exec\u001b[22m, but the specified command is run from the subdirectory containing the matched file, which is not normally the direc‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 534/1271 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              tory in which you started \u001b[1mfind\u001b[22m.  As with -exec, the {} should be quoted if find is being invoked from a shell.  This a much more\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 535/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              secure  method for invoking commands, as it avoids race conditions during resolution of the paths to the matched files.  As with\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 536/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the \u001b[1m-exec \u001b[22maction, the `+' form of \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[22mwill build a command line to process more than one matched file, but any given  invo‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 537/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              cation  of  \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m will only list files that exist in the same subdirectory.  If you use this option, you must ensure that your\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 538/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[1mPATH \u001b[22menvironment variable does not reference `.'; otherwise, an attacker can run any commands they like by leaving an  appropri‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 539/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ately-named  file  in a directory in which you will run \u001b[1m-execdir\u001b[22m.  The same applies to having entries in \u001b[1mPATH \u001b[22mwhich are empty or\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 540/1271 50% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.523133, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              which are not absolute directory names.  If any invocation with the `+' form returns a non-zero value as exit status, then  \u001b[1mfind\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 541/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.523339, "o", "              returns  a  non-zero exit status.  If \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mencounters an error, this can sometimes cause an immediate exit, so some pending com‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 542/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              mands may not be run at all.  The result of the action depends on whether the \u001b[1m+ \u001b[22mor the \u001b[1m; \u001b[22mvariant is  being  used;  \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcom‐\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 543/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              \u001b[4mmand\u001b[24m \u001b[1m{} + \u001b[22malways returns true, while \u001b[1m-execdir \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcommand\u001b[24m \u001b[1m{} ; \u001b[22mreturns true only if \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m returns 0.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 544/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 545/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.523486, "o", "       -fls \u001b[4mfile\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 546/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              True;  like \u001b[1m-ls \u001b[22mbut write to \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m like \u001b[1m-fprint\u001b[22m.  The output file is always created, even if the predicate is never matched.  See\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 547/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              the \u001b[1mUNUSUAL FILENAMES \u001b[22msection for information about how unusual characters in filenames are handled.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 548/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 549/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -fprint \u001b[4mfile\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 550/1271 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.523625, "o", "              True; print the full file name into file \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m.  If \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m does not exist when \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mis run, it is created; if it does exist, it  is\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 551/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.523759, "o", "              truncated.  The file names \u001b[4m/dev/stdout\u001b[24m and \u001b[4m/dev/stderr\u001b[24m are handled specially; they refer to the standard output and standard er‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 552/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ror output, respectively.  The output file is always created, even if the predicate is never matched.  See the \u001b[1mUNUSUAL FILENAMES\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 553/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              section for information about how unusual characters in filenames are handled.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 554/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 555/1271 52% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
