[2071.62301, "o", "              A `%' character followed by any other character is discarded, but the other character is printed (don't rely on this, as further\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 775/1271 66% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.623083, "o", "              format characters may be introduced).  A `%' at the end of the format argument causes undefined behaviour since there is no fol‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 776/1271 66% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.636873, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              lowing  character.  In some locales, it may hide your door keys, while in others it may remove the final page from the novel you\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 777/1271 66% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.637177, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              are reading.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 778/1271 66% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 779/1271 66% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.637444, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              The %m and %d directives support the \u001b[1m#\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m0 \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m+ \u001b[22mflags, but the other directives do not, even if they print numbers.  Numeric di‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 780/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              rectives that do not support these flags include \u001b[1mG\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mU\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mb\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mD\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mk \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mn\u001b[22m.  The `-' format flag is supported and changes  the  align‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 781/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              ment of a field from right-justified (which is the default) to left-justified.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 782/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 783/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.637678, "o", "              See the \u001b[1mUNUSUAL FILENAMES \u001b[22msection for information about how unusual characters in filenames are handled.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 784/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 785/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -prune True;  if  the file is a directory, do not descend into it.  If \u001b[1m-depth \u001b[22mis given, then \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mhas no effect.  Because \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22mim‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 786/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              plies \u001b[1m-depth\u001b[22m, you cannot usefully use \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-delete \u001b[22mtogether.  For example, to skip the directory \u001b[4msrc/emacs\u001b[24m and  all  files\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 787/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.637974, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              and directories under it, and print the names of the other files found, do something like this:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 788/1271 67% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  find . -path ./src/emacs -prune -o -print\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 789/1271 68% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 790/1271 68% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.638237, "o", "       -quit  Exit  immediately  (with return value zero if no errors have occurred).  This is different to \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22mbecause \u001b[1m-prune \u001b[22monly applies\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 791/1271 68% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              to the contents of pruned directories, while \u001b[1m-quit \u001b[22msimply makes \u001b[1mfind \u001b[22mstop immediately.  No child processes will be left running.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 792/1271 68% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Any command lines which have been built by \u001b[1m-exec ... + \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-execdir ... + \u001b[22mare invoked before the program is exited.  After  \u001b[1m-quit\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 793/1271 68% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.638446, "o", "              is  executed, no more files specified on the command line will be processed.  For example, `\u001b[1mfind \u001b[4m\u001b[22m/tmp/foo\u001b[24m \u001b[4m/tmp/bar\u001b[24m \u001b[1m-print -quit\u001b[22m`\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 794/1271 68% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.65414, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              will print only `/tmp/foo`.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 795/1271 68% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              One common use of \u001b[1m-quit \u001b[22mis to stop searching the file system once we have found what we want.  For example, if we want  to  find\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 796/1271 68% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.654273, "o", "              just a single file we can do this:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 797/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K                  find / -name needle -print -quit\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 798/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 799/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.654365, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1mOPERATORS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 800/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.654448, "o", "       Listed in order of decreasing precedence:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 801/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.655035, "o", "\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 802/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       ( \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[24m )\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 803/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Force  precedence.   Since  parentheses are special to the shell, you will normally need to quote them.  Many of the examples in\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 804/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              this manual page use backslashes for this purpose: `\\(...\\)' instead of `(...)'.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 805/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[2071.671121, "o", "\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 806/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       ! \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[24m True if \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[24m is false.  This character will also usually need protection from interpretation by the shell.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 807/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 808/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       -not \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 809/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.671299, "o", "              Same as ! \u001b[4mexpr\u001b[24m, but not POSIX compliant.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 810/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 811/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K       \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 812/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.671417, "o", "              Two expressions in a row are taken to be joined with an implied \u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m; \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[24m is not evaluated if \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m is false.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 813/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 814/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
[2071.67153, "o", "       \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m -a \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 815/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K              Same as \u001b[4mexpr1\u001b[24m \u001b[4mexpr2\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page find(1) line 816/1271 69% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K\r\u001b[K \u001b[KESC\b\b\bESC\u001b[KO\bO\u001b[KB\bB\r\u001b[K"]
